          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ce1d09850c8d25508d9c99ff2e15235cf1d53d0a",
          "message": "feat(skills): panel-review reuse pair default-on + ponytail reuse ladder (#242)\n\n* feat(skills): panel-review reuse pair default-on + ponytail reuse ladder\n\nThe panel-review skill was gating library-reuse-reviewer and\ncode-duplication-reviewer on narrow surface signals ('only when a\nnew dependency is added' / 'only when actual duplication shape is\npresent'). This is backwards: the whole job of these agents is to\nFIND the duplication and the reinvented stdlib that ISN'T obvious\nfrom the diff surface. Gating them on the signal already being\nvisible skipped them on exactly the diffs where they add the most\nvalue — the panel ended up not calling the code-reuse agents.\n\nFix: make the reuse pair DEFAULT-ON for any non-trivial code diff\n(not pure-docs / pure-config). They default to silence when they\nfind nothing, so the cost of a false-positive inclusion is low\n(one quiet agent); the cost of a false-negative exclusion is a\nshipped over-build.\n\nAdopted from Ponytail (https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail):\n- The 7-rung reuse ladder (Does this need to exist? -> Already in\n  codebase? -> Stdlib? -> Native platform? -> Installed dep? ->\n  One line? -> Minimum) as a structured brief for the reuse pair.\n- The delete:/stdlib:/native:/yagni:/shrink: tag vocabulary for\n  uniform, actionable findings.\n- The 'net: -<N> lines possible.' score — a concrete countable\n  metric for the reuse axis instead of generic prose.\n- Root-cause discipline (grep every caller, fix the shared function\n  once) added to both the Spec subagent brief and the reuse brief.\n\nStructural: extracted the reuse-ladder brief and the Step 9 output\ntemplate into references/ to keep SKILL.md under the 500-line\nguideline (499 lines, down from a would-be 596). Fixed a\ndescription/body contradiction on pure-docs diffs (description said\n'NOT for pure-docs'; body said 'pure-docs skip Domain, Spec may\nstill run' — kept the body behaviour, dropped pure-docs from the\nnegative scope).\n\n* refactor(skills): strip ponytail provenance from panel-review skill body\n\nProvenance is useless to the agent consuming the skill — it doesn't\nhelp it review better, and 'Ponytail' is an undefined term to a fresh\ncontext. Attribution belongs in the commit message, not the skill body.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(docs): add onward links from panel-review references to fix matlatl dead-end gate\n\nThe two extracted reference files (output-template.md, reuse-ladder.md)\nhad inbound links from SKILL.md but no onward links, so matlatl v0.0.5\nunder --strict flagged them as dead-end documents (structureFindingsSeverity:\nwarning promotes the finding to a failure). The existing reference file\nconfig-format.md already follows the convention of ending with a\n[← back to the skill](../SKILL.md) link; apply the same to both new\nfiles. Regenerated llms.txt (1348->1350 refs, 2->0 dead-ends).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>",
