          "id": "38d28e0f19cac092760b0fd6cda65f4cdeb5aade",
          "message": "ci(site): add purge_before_sync dispatch option to force full re-upload (#301)\n\n`aws s3 sync` compares size/mtime, so it won't re-PUT objects after a\nbucket-level change it can't see — notably a switch of the bucket's\nserver-side encryption (existing objects keep their old SSE). Adds an\noptional workflow_dispatch boolean that empties the bucket before the\nsync, forcing every object to be re-uploaded fresh under the current\nbucket settings. Default false; normal push-to-main deploys are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-24T07:44:08+03:00",
