          "id": "3abdd3283af6af9f7e62a06684faeb7c882d6f7b",
          "message": "fix(plan): mechanical follow-ups from the PR-293 post-merge review (#297)\n\nAddresses only the MECHANICAL findings from the post-merge review of the\nplan-approval gate (issue #206 / PR #293). The design-loaded findings\n(approve-then-cancel mode-flip loss, disconnect durable-log-tail drop,\ncontinuation-logic dedup) are deliberately left for separate decisions.\n\n- server/http.go: planModeFromString lowercases BEFORE trimming the\n  PERMISSION_MODE_ prefix, so the documented case-insensitive spelling\n  (\"permission_mode_default\") is honoured instead of silently falling\n  through to deny/iterate.\n- server/service.go: autoApproveWaitTimeout var -> const (never overridden;\n  matches its sibling const autoApprovePollInterval).\n- app/build.go: --plan-mode-auto-approve on an INTERACTIVE deployment now\n  WARNs it is INERT (the flag only fires headless), mirroring\n  normalizeAskReviewerModel's inert-when-interactive posture, instead of\n  narrating a \"NO HUMAN REVIEW\" fact that does nothing.\n- mecatui/ui/view.go: the footer \"W auto-accept\" hint is gated on\n  ask.offerAlways, matching the action bar; a surfaced child plan ask\n  (offerAlways=false) no longer advertises a key that no-ops.\n- permconfig: new plan_mode_auto_approve_test.go pins the operator-tier-only\n  boundary (a project-tier plan-mode-auto-approve: is ignored with a WARN) —\n  the one operator-tier scalar whose boundary was previously untested.\n- adr/0069: amendment note recording the deny path terminates via\n  StopPlanIterate (superseded the ADR's \"loop continues\" design; frozen ADR\n  corrected by note, not rewritten in place).\n\nNOTE: llms.txt must be regenerated (task docs:llms) after the ADR edit; the\nsandbox could not fetch the matlatl module to do so here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
