          "id": "25594361a1baff5adc7f36657058293baf31af61",
          "message": "feat(mecatui): dynamic terminal window/tab title from session title + phase (#303)\n\nEvery mecatui tab showed the static title \"mecatui\", making multiple\nsessions in a tab bar indistinguishable. The window title is now\n\"<session title> — <status word> mecatui\":\n\n  fix the login redirect bug — Working mecatui   (running)\n  fix the login redirect bug — ⚠ mecatui         (awaiting approval)\n  fix the login redirect bug — mecatui           (idle)\n  mecatui                                        (no title yet / opt-out)\n\nThe title leads because tab bars truncate from the right; the status is\na static word (never an animated spinner — per-frame title churn trips\nOS attention heuristics). The session title reuses the engine's existing\nset-once session Title (the first genuine prompt): seeded locally in\nsubmitPrompt, adopted from the /sessions picker on switch, and\nself-healed via the existing GetSession refetch (ResolvedModelMsg now\ncarries Title) for carryover/fork/adopt paths. Client-side only — no\nproto/engine/server changes.\n\nOpt-out: --terminal-title=off or MECATUI_NO_TERMINAL_TITLE=1.\n\nAlso hardens sanitizeTerminal to strip the C1 control range (0x80-0x9F —\n8-bit CSI/OSC equivalents) in addition to C0/ESC/DEL, closing a\ndefence-in-depth CWE-150 gap on the window-title path (panel security\nreview).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
