          "id": "da4fdcb08f5283eefbfdd81a317ca1e771f7295f",
          "message": "test(osfs): make TestMatchReadRoot_Lexical host-independent (#357)\n\n#353 made MatchReadRoot normalize the path's top-level alias (macOS\n/var -> /private/var, Fedora /srv -> /var/srv) while comparing against\nthe root verbatim. Production roots are canonical by construction\n(WithReadRoots canonicalizes at construction), but the test fed a\nhard-coded lexical /srv/skills/demo root, which mismatches its own\npaths on hosts where /srv is a symlink (e.g. Fedora Silverblue).\n\nFeed a root under t.TempDir() (canonical on every host) and add\nTestMatchReadRoot_TopLevelAlias pinning the issue-#356 contract: an\nalias-written path matches a canonical root, and a lexical root never\nsilently matches canonical paths. The new test runs only on hosts with\na top-level system alias and skips elsewhere.\n\nFixes #356\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>",
