          "id": "8d187f07367c7f1ae45d33d71700beafe928ef81",
          "message": "feat(bash): background commands via background:true + BashStatus (#361)\n\n* feat(osfs): kill the process group on command cancel; add CommandStreamer\n\nThe osfs CommandRunner used exec.CommandContext with no SysProcAttr, so\nctx cancel SIGKILLed only the direct sh and orphaned grandchildren (a\ncancelled make left its compilers behind). Extract the hookexec\nprocess-group discipline into internal/adapter/procgroup and wire it\ninto the shared spawn tail — foreground Bash gets the fix too.\n\nAdd the optional tool.CommandStreamer interface (RunStreaming to a\ncaller-owned io.Writer) for bounded tail capture; osfs implements it\nover the same private run tail so Run and RunStreaming cannot drift.\nEngine API: Added/minor (task api:update + CHANGELOG).\n\nPart of #23 (background commands).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(bash): background commands via background:true + BashStatus\n\nThe commands half of #23: a background flag on the existing Bash tool\n(the governance evaluator special-cases the literal name, so a new tool\nname would bypass the permission gate) returns immediately with a\nbashcmd-<id> job id; the command runs detached in the real workspace\nunder the same pre-dispatch permission classification as foreground\nBash. BashStatus is the sole output/cancel channel: roster (ids + stop\nlabels only), per-job command + bounded 64 KiB output tail, wait_ms,\nand a cancel verb that rides the new process-group kill.\n\nJobs ride the child-run registry as the non-delegation bash-cmd family\n— no child session/engine/events — reusing the run-end drain/seal, the\nfamily-aware turn-boundary notice, and the pending nudge. Children\n(Subagent/explorer/members) get background-capable Bash against their\nown run registry, never BashStatus. Run-scoped v1; Ctrl+B mid-flight\ndetach, session-scoped detach, and wire events are follow-ups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs: ADR 0090 background Bash + living docs + user docs\n\nADR 0090 records the design: flag-on-Bash (the evaluator special-cases\nthe literal name — a new name is a permission bypass), the engine/agent\ntool over the childCapableTool seam, real-workspace/no-isolation, the\nnon-delegation registry family, CommandStreamer + bounded tail, the\nprocgroup pre-fix, run-scoped v1 with named deferrals.\n\nArchitecture, implementation notes, production-readiness (issue #23\ncommands half shipped), usage reference, and the public core-tools page\nupdated; llms.txt regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>",
