          "id": "d17cd073f9e06561a4a5d3cc62733a247fc11b8a",
          "message": "ci(provider): standalone gate offline + cover anthropic; exclude SA5011 test-file false positives\n\n* ci(provider): run the standalone gate offline — cover anthropic, no credential\n\nThe previous job was scoped to ssefilter only, on the theory that anthropic\nneeds git credentials to fetch engine v0.8.0 (mecatl is private, so\nproxy.golang.org 404s it and a networked GOWORK=off fetch 401s). But the gate\ndoesn't need the network at all: run it GOPROXY=off over a module cache warmed\nfrom the committed go.sum, and every dependency must already be local — no\ncredential, no private-fetch surface, and a STRONGER guarantee (offline, not\njust off-workspace).\n\nanthropic now qualifies (engine v0.8.0 is cache-resolvable once warmed), so the\ngate covers ssefilter + anthropic. openai + openaichat stay excluded only\nbecause they require provider/ssefilter v0.0.0, which no cache can resolve\nuntil the first provider/ssefilter tag — tracked in #379. Adds a GOPROXY var to\ntask test:provider-standalone (default networked locally, GOPROXY=off in CI) so\nthe offline form reproduces with ok  \tgithub.com/stacklok/mecatl/provider/ssefilter\t(cached)\nok  \tgithub.com/stacklok/mecatl/provider/anthropic\t(cached).\nADR 0093 updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* ci(provider): warm the standalone cache with read-only auth, gate offline\n\nThe offline-only warm was unsound: engine v0.8.0 must be fetched from the\nprivate origin, which needs auth (proxy.golang.org can't serve a private\nmodule), and 'go mod download' doesn't resolve the full build/test graph anyway.\nWarm the module cache with the workflow's read-only GITHUB_TOKEN (an insteadOf\nrewrite scoped to the warm step, dropped right after), then run the gate fully\noffline (GOPROXY=off) so the self-contained proof never touches the network and\ncarries no credential. ADR 0093 updated to record that the warm needs auth on a\nprivate repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* ci(lint): exclude staticcheck SA5011 in test files — deterministic false positive\n\nThe SA5011 'possible nil pointer dereference' findings failing CI are false\npositives on the idiomatic test guard 'if x == nil { t.Fatal(...) }; use(x)'.\nstaticcheck computes t.Fatal's no-return facts over the whole program, and on\nthe 2-core CI runner they come back incomplete — flagging a rolling subset of\nthe ~117 test files using the idiom (authfile, models, cliconfig, mcpserver,\n…) while golangci-lint reports 0 issues locally with the identical v2.12.2 +\nconfig. GOGC/concurrency/GOMEMLIMIT tuning and a bigger runner (not\nprovisioned) could not make it deterministic, and per-site edits across 117\nfiles are the wrong answer to a checker-environment divergence. Exclude SA5011\nin *_test.go (production code keeps the check at full strength), matching the\nrepo's existing test-file relaxation block. Config verified; task lint green\nacross all modules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>",
