          "id": "10e7b876ca1655e2922b8e571a9104f73690605c",
          "message": "fix(mecatui): restore capabilities on /sessions continue + /effort fork, block gated slash sends (#348) (#389)\n\nThree same-family bugs left a mecatui session with zero client\ncapabilities, so every caps-gated builtin (/models, /effort, /mcp, ...)\nvanished from the palette and a typed /models fell through to the model\nas a costly prose prompt:\n\n1. switchToSession zeroed m.caps and the continue handoff\n   (continueLoadedSession) never restored them — the adopted session had\n   no CreateSession in this process, so no SessionReadyMsg ever arrived.\n2. switchEffortCmd explicitly returned an empty-capabilities\n   SessionReadyMsg after an /effort fork.\n3. A bare slash line matching no available builtin was sent to the model\n   as an ordinary prompt.\n\nFix:\n- Session proto gains ServerCapabilities capabilities = 11; GetSession\n  and SetMode populate it from the same Service.capabilities() value\n  CreateSession echoes (nil-safe: older servers omit the field, the\n  client reads it through the nil-safe generated getter).\n- The client surfaces it on SessionSnapshot/ResolvedModelMsg;\n  continueLoadedSession now fires RefreshResolvedModelCmd (the heal\n  round-trip the footer heal already uses) and onResolvedModelMsg adopts\n  non-zero caps — an all-zero struct means a pre-#348 server, so prior\n  caps are kept (fail-conservative).\n- switchToSession keeps the prior caps until the heal lands: no\n  dead-builtins window; pinned by TestSwitchToSessionPreservesCaps.\n- switchEffortCmd populates SessionReadyMsg.Capabilities from the\n  post-fork GetSession snapshot.\n- interceptSlashCommand: a bare line naming a KNOWN builtin that is\n  gated off is blocked (input kept, warning status, case-insensitive) —\n  it never reaches the model; unknown slash names still fall through.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
