          "id": "75fe1e4b2c069d080cb9dac1b8bd6b6c9a49a1c9",
          "message": "fix(mecatui): bound embedded shutdown on in-flight scheduled fires (#388) (#390)\n\nQuitting embedded mecatui while a scheduled fire ran could hang the\nprocess indefinitely (Ctrl+C printed ^C but never killed it). Shutdown\nis now bounded at every layer with a hard-stop fallback and a\nsecond-signal force exit:\n\n- embed.Server.Close: gRPC GracefulStop bounded (30s) + grpc.Stop()\n  fallback; composition teardown bounded (10s); socket/dir always removed.\n- Scheduler.Stop: leadership-loop + epoch joins bounded (5s each, WARN on\n  abandon); fire grace unchanged.\n- Service.Close: cancels in-flight runs via run.Cancel, EXCLUDING runs\n  parked on a permission ask whose durable awaiting snapshot is the\n  cloud-native Phase-2 resume point (race-free runState.awaiting atomic,\n  set by Persist only after the durable Save lands); per-session engine\n  close bounded (10s).\n- mcp.Manager.Close: bounded (5s).\n- cmd/mecatui: two-signal handler owns sigCh as its sole consumer (no\n  signal.Stop on the force-exit path) so a second SIGINT/SIGTERM during\n  cleanup deterministically hard-exits os.Exit(130); the whole post-quit\n  cleanup is capped at 45s and the handler retires only after cleanup\n  completes (no force-exit race).\n- scheduler_fire: a shutdown-cancelled fire's session is persisted\n  terminal (cancelled, Interrupt-recoverable) and RecordFire stores the\n  real fire id, never \"pending\".\n\nTests: per-piece unit tests plus an offline e2e (shutdown_e2e_test.go)\nthat blocks a scheduled fire in an LLM call and proves Close returns\nwithin the bound with the fire persisted terminal. Mirrors the mecak8s\nbounded-shutdown precedent. ADR-0027 re-audit: no new resource row.",
