          "id": "f8706c4c1f52cb3b43b339fe95ba6ba5685f8512",
          "message": "fix(mecatui): reconnect the live session feed + recover missed schedule notifications (#387) (#392)\n\n* fix(mecatui): reconnect the live session feed + recover missed schedule notifications (#387)\n\nThe mecatui per-session StreamSessionLive feed silently died on a clean\nclose or transient error: updateLiveMsg cleared the channel refs and\nreturned, with no reconnect and no operator signal. After a server\nrestart / gRPC failure / proxy idle timeout / network interruption the\nUI looked healthy while its fire-result notification path was dead, and\na correctly-persisted fire result could be missed until a manual reload.\n\nThe feed now self-heals, entirely client-side (no engine-port or proto\nchange — ADR 0096):\n\n- client.ReconnectLiveCmd/reconnectLiveLoop: a bounded exponential-\n  backoff loop (500ms base, x2, 30s cap, +/-20% jitter) that, per\n  attempt, drains the durable catch-up via the EXISTING\n  StreamSessionEvents full replay (recovering a delivery note emitted\n  during the gap) then re-opens StreamSessionLive. Stops on ctx cancel\n  (session switch / TUI exit).\n- Exactly-once is a client-side FireID dedup, not a server cursor: the\n  ui's seenFireIDs set (keyed on DeliveryNoteMsg.FireID) suppresses a\n  note that arrives via BOTH the catch-up and the re-opened live feed;\n  applyDeliveryNote is the single dedup site both paths funnel through.\n- A concise degraded footer cue (\"live feed reconnecting (attempt N)…\")\n  replaces the silent drop; cleared on reconnect.\n- The reconnect loop gets its own generation guard (liveReconGen) so a\n  stale reader after a session switch is dropped without reconnecting\n  the old session; a duplicate concurrent reconnect for the same\n  session is refused.\n- The fenced delivery discriminator is unchanged (regression-pinned: an\n  un-fenced \"[scheduled task …\" prompt is never misclassified).\n\nThe full-replay-per-reconnect is O(log) not O(gap); accepted (the real\ngap is a handful of buffered events). The server-side from_seq cursor\nis the documented upgrade path if a deployment proves it hot (ADR 0096).\n\nTests: client reconnect_test.go (trigger/retry/cancel/catch-up/backoff\nbounds/discriminator) + ui reconnect_live_test.go (close+error trigger,\ndedup-across-paths, session-switch stop, no-duplicate, degraded footer,\nunfenced-prompt regression). Docs: ADR 0096, IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES,\nuser-docs scheduled-tasks.\n\n* fix(mecatui): stop reconnect loop on disabled backoff instead of hot-spin (#387)\n\nReview finding L1: a non-positive base backoff made liveReconnectDelay\nreturn 0, and the prior else-if arm only returned when ctx was already\ndone — so a disabled backoff busy-spun the reconnect loop. Now the d<=0\narm returns immediately, and a test pins the no-spin behaviour.\n\n* fix(mecatui): scope live-feed catch-up to delivery notes, add transcript-dedup regression (#387)\n\nThe catch-up replay is a full historical scan; updateReconnectMsg must\nreduce only DeliveryNoteMsg from it and drop every other event, or a\nreconnect re-renders the entire prior transcript into the live\nconversation (the spec-review finding). Adds\nTestReconnectUI_CatchUpDoesNotDuplicateTranscript pinning that a replayed\nturn/delta/tool/prompt/result never lands in m.conv while the delivery\nnote does. Refines ADR 0096's accepted-costs wording to match the\nas-built delivery-only forwarder.",
