          "id": "fca44784b3ed47aaa7d89d169473372f193ad199",
          "message": "feat(agent): surface permanent provider errors so a doomed retry says so (#346) (#401)\n\nA run failing on a PERMANENT provider rejection (4xx other than 408/429 —\ninvalid_encrypted_content, a policy-blocked model, a malformed request\nshape baked into the persisted history) ended the session 'failed' with a\nraw provider-error wall. Session.Recover made retry POSSIBLE, but a\npermanent-cause failure replays byte-identically and re-fails forever,\nwith nothing telling the user the session is unrecoverable-by-retry.\n\nThread a neutral permanence bit end to end:\n\n- engine/port: PermanentError interface (error + Permanent() bool) —\n  rides the error chain via errors.As, never a port.LLMRequest field, so\n  engine/agent stays provider-neutral. Fail-open: an unclassifiable error\n  is NOT permanent.\n- internal/adapter/llmresilience: wrap surfaced non-retryable errors\n  (establishment + mid-stream) in permanentError; breaker/exhausted/\n  idle/cancel paths never wrapped.\n- provider/{openai,anthropic,openaichat}: stream errors implement\n  Permanent() — context-overflow message OR (status!=0 AND non-retryable);\n  408/429/5xx/unknown fail open. Error() text byte-identical.\n- engine/session: ResultPayload.Permanent; Session.RecordFailurePermanence\n  /FailurePermanence (StateFailed-only, cleared on Recover); sessnap\n  Snapshot.Permanent round-trips; eventsource fold reconstructs the flag\n  (store.go MUST round-trip list updated).\n- engine/agent: permanentCause threads the bit through terminate →\n  emitResult → Result.Permanent (terminateComplete/ChunkDone stays false —\n  no Go error to classify).\n- internal/adapter/server: proto Result.permanent=5; on re-entry to a\n  permanently-failed session, emit a once-per-recovery EvRecoverNotice\n  advisory before the run (recoverNotices, swept on CloseSession). Recover\n  stays unblocked — advisory, not a gate.\n- cmd/mecatui: Result.Permanent decodes (forces Transient=false; legacy\n  transientVocab kept as the old-server fallback); a permanent StopError\n  renders a one-line sanitized summary (collapses the openai POST/JSON\n  envelope) with the raw payload behind ctrl+t; the recover notice renders\n  as a durable scrollback warning block.\n\nADR 0097 records the contract (neutral interface over a new StopReason;\nfail-open; Recover-unblocked; the event-vs-conversation-note channel).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
