          "id": "72c04dd39f9bc86e26a09e378936837c13b1153f",
          "message": "refactor(mecatui): approval modal consolidation (#555 Phase 1) (#608)\n\n* refactor(mecatui): carve approval modal into domain-owned files (#555 Phase 1)\n\nThe approval modal's state and behavior were scattered across six files split\nby technical layer (model.go fields, update.go reducers, permission.go\nrenderers, clickgeom.go hit-test, view.go render arm, keys.go bindings). That\nspread is the drift point PR #553 exposed — a single feature touched the\nrender path and the hit-test arm in two places and got them out of sync.\n\nPhase 1 consolidates the modal into four domain-owned files, no behavior\nchange:\n\n- approval_state.go — the approvalState value (ask, FIFO queue, dedupe set,\n  plan/args viewport clusters) and its pure queue-manipulation methods.\n  Model now holds ONE `approval approvalState` field instead of ~12 loose\n  fields; resetSession/endRun collapse to approval.reset().\n- approval_surface.go — the reducers/handlers, split into a pure surface half\n  (mutates approvalState, returns []approvalAction) and thin Model shims that\n  execute the actions (the wire send, the transcript notice, the phase\n  transition, the spinner re-arm). The modal no longer calls the wire\n  directly — the surface proposes, the Model disposes. approvalDeps is the\n  explicit five-field list of what the surface may touch, built per call,\n  never stored; no *Model back-reference.\n- approval_render.go — the renderers/builders (formerly permission.go) +\n  renderApprovalBody.\n- approval_regions.go — the mouse hit-test geometry.\n\nThe keymap bindings (Allow/Deny/RawArgs) stay Model-global vocabulary; the\nphase value and the phase<->ask invariant stay Model-side.\n\nStructural gate: approval_arch_test.go fails CI if an approval-vocabulary\ndeclaration lands outside the four files, or if Model grows a second\napprovalState field.\n\nVerification: task test, task lint, task docs all green; the frame goldens\nTestViewGoldenStripped/TestViewGoldenAztecANSI pass unmodified; the\nspinner re-arm contract (TestResolveLastAskRearmsSpinner,\nTestSpinnerVisibleMatchesFooterRender) is intact. go run ./cmd/mecademo\nprints the full offline session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* refactor(mecatui): dedupe approval resume clamp; stdlib min/max/slices (#555 review)\n\nPanel-review follow-up to Phase 1. The cross-confirmed Domain finding:\napprovalState.advance() already clamps adv.resume to idle|running, and the\nthree Model-side consumers re-applied the identical `if resume != phaseIdle {\nresume = phaseRunning }` — one resume invariant living in four places, dead\ncode that would silently diverge if the rule ever changed. Delete the three\nconsumer copies and trust advance()'s contract (the single source of truth).\n\nMechanical cleanups from the same pass:\n- miniScroll + permissionModalBodyParts clamps → max(0, min(...)) builtins.\n- askQueueIndex → slices.IndexFunc.\n- drop the dead Model markAskResolved shim (only a test used it; it now calls\n  approvalState.markAskResolved directly).\n- fix the arch-gate regex's dead advanceAsk token (the symbol is advance()).\n\napprovalAction's open-* payload (ask/queued/model) is deliberately KEPT: it\nmakes the action self-describing for any future non-immediate dispatch (the\nout-of-order-approval direction discussed in review), at the cost of a\ntoday-redundant copy. Documented in the PR.\n\ntask test / task lint green; goldens unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* test(mecatui): pin the three approval invariants the goldens miss (#555 review)\n\nThe QA/test-adequacy pass on Phase 1 found three behaviors the frame goldens\ndo not pin — axes a \"pure migration\" could silently break while the suite\nstays green. Add executable oracles for each:\n\n- TestPlanReviewNoOpRepopulationPreservesOffset / TestArgsViewRawToggleRepopulates:\n  the planVP/argsVP fingerprint no-op-repopulation guard (a dropped fingerprint\n  would re-SetContent and yank the operator's reading position, invisible to a\n  single-frame golden). Verified the plan test FAILS when the guard's\n  fingerprint term is removed, so it pins the behavior, not just the code.\n- TestDebugAskResolveNilStreamNoPanic: the /debug-ask-from-idle nil-stream\n  resolve path — the sendApproval dep must return nil, not panic, and the\n  notice must still land. The one path no golden executes.\n- TestPhaseAskIDBiconditional: the documented `phase==phaseAwaitingApproval ⟺\n  ask.AskID != \"\"` invariant swept across open / enqueue / resolve-successor /\n  resolve-drain / retract-visible. The arch gate is placement-only; this is the\n  behavioral pin.\n\ntask test / task lint green; goldens unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
