          "id": "c605ea0fec37bf664ae2f9ad6fccf23fa609bdaf",
          "message": "feat(mecak8s): add local Yardstick vMCP qualification fixture (#742)\n\n* feat(mecak8s): add local Yardstick vMCP fixture\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(oidc): add scoped private HTTPS issuer and diagnostics\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(mecak8s): wire TLS and OIDC Helm values\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(mecak8s): split vMCP OIDC/TLS overlay out of values-kind.yaml\n\ne2e/k8s's Ginkgo suite installs the chart with values-kind.yaml alone and\n--wait, creating no Secrets/ConfigMaps beyond the namespace. The oidc/tls\nblocks added there required dex-fixture-ca and mecak8s-tls, which only the\nmecak8s-vmcp fixture's own setup creates — the e2e pod hung mounting a\nmissing volume until the install timed out (CI: k8s e2e (kind), PR #742).\n\nMove those blocks into a new values-kind-vmcp.yaml overlay that only\ndeploy/mecak8s-vmcp/Taskfile.yml layers on top; values-kind.yaml goes back\nto being Redis-only. Adds a regression test pinning the bare-file shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(mecak8s): follow the OIDC overlay split in deploycheck tests\n\ninternal/deploycheck/vmcp_test.go read values-kind.yaml directly for the\nOIDC/TLS fields moved to values-kind-vmcp.yaml in 52c8add5, breaking\nTestMecak8sVMCPPOC_Scenario3_OIDCNegativeCases and\n..._NoScopeEnforcement (CI: Test (race root complement)). Read both files;\nalso assert the Taskfile layers the new overlay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
