          "id": "aea3342c936ef735564afdf5f8f5ef8b5e78facb",
          "message": "docs: ADR 0252 — HTTP steer endpoint (#874)\n\n* docs: ADR 0252 — HTTP steer endpoint\n\nExtends ADR 0232's named deferral: POST /v1/sessions/{id}/steer +\nsteer-cancel, mirroring approve/cancel, reusing the RFC 9457 registry\nfor stale-control rejection. No engine change — pure transport\naddition over the existing Service.Steer/Service.CancelSteer calls.\n\nDocs only; implementation tracked separately.\n\nRefs #873, #821.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address review feedback on ADR 0252\n\nPer samuv's review: fix the promoted-run wedge (drain via the same\napprove-handler REHYDRATE precedent instead of handing back a bare\nrun_id), carry multimodal parts in the request contract (ADR 0251),\nadd a feature-registry row instead of discover-by-404ing (PR #823),\nand rename steer-cancel to cancel-steer to match the cancel-child\nverb-first convention.\n\nFully or partially written by an AI agent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate llms.txt after rebase\n\n* docs: spell out the two distinct stale-run-control refusals\n\nPer samuv's review thread on the 409 bullet: name both refusal\npaths funneling through stale_run_control explicitly (an\nexpected_run_id naming a non-current run, and strict steer's\ndeliberate non-promotion on a terminal named run) rather than\nleaving the second implicit.\n\nFully or partially written by an AI agent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: name the shared media validation/capability path for steer parts\n\nPer samuv's review thread: state explicitly that steer parts reuse\ntoContentParts/session.NewContent/ValidateMediaParts and the same\nProviderCapabilities() gate as the ACP prompt path, not a second\nvalidation path.\n\nFully or partially written by an AI agent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
