          "id": "0f31e2f8d123f3e85078f8848331e4e9cd4c4e1f",
          "message": "docs: ADR 0253 — SDK mocking testkit (#875)\n\n* docs: ADR 0253 — SDK mocking testkit\n\nVendor (not npm-depend on) the proven unary Connect-RPC handler\npattern + AutoAPIMock core; defer streaming/bidi mocking (Converse,\nthe stale-run-control race) as a named residual. Lives inside\nmecatl's own SDK tree for now, no shared package yet.\n\nDocs only; implementation tracked separately.\n\nRefs #872.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address review feedback on ADR 0253, rebase onto main\n\nPer samuv's review: fix the \"over HTTP\" transport category error\n(the vendored automocker covers unary gRPC, not the hand-written\nJSON HTTP endpoints), name the sdk/typescript/ ordering dependency\non #821 and the missing TS CI gate, correct #618's tense (open, not\nmerged) and adopt its SPDX-guard pattern scoped to sdk/, and record\nthe header rewrite as an authorized relicense (Stacklok holds\ncopyright on both sides) rather than a bare header edit.\n\nAlso reframes scope explicitly: the SDK's own testability (near-term\ndeadline) and Studio's eventual HTTP/JSON mocking needs (later,\narchitecture undecided) are separate, coexisting concerns. This ADR\nonly needs to unblock the former.\n\nRebased onto main (#874 merged) and regenerated llms.txt.\n\nFully or partially written by an AI agent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
