          "id": "55e18081f16eea4ea69d5b439cd7be68fc4b33dd",
          "message": "feat: scheduled tasks — Phase 2b: settings.yaml schedules + CLI management + metrics (#233) (#238)\n\n* feat(scheduler): Phase 2b — settings.yaml schedules block (operator-tier) + declarative reconcile\n\nAdd an operator-tier-only 'schedules:' block to settings.yaml, mirroring the\nguardrails operator-tier-only discipline: capture from user-global + CLI tiers\nonly, WARN + ignore on project-tier, strict unknown-key parse per declaration.\n\n- internal/adapter/permconfig/schema.go: SchedulesSection (YAML sequence) +\n  ScheduleDecl (strict strictFields/UnmarshalYAML), top-level Config field\n- internal/adapter/permconfig/resolve.go: operatorSchedules field +\n  captureSchedules (first-non-nil, CLI outranks user-global) +\n  OperatorSchedules() accessor + project-tier WARN\n- internal/app/schedules.go: foldOperatorSchedules + toScheduleSpec mapper\n  (defaults Mode=plan for non-mutating; fail-soft per decl) +\n  reconcileSchedules (idempotent upsert; no delete — documented)\n- internal/app/build.go: DeclaredSchedules cfg field + fold + reconcile after\n  scheduler start, gated on SchedulerEnabled\n- internal/adapter/server/schedule.go: UpdateSchedule preserves CreatedAt\n  (pre-existing bug amplified by the reconcile path)\n- configgen: schedules subtree (TierOperator, ListBody) + skeleton/reference\n- Tests: operator-tier honoured, project ignored, strict-key, CLI outranks,\n  reconcile idempotency (singleton:false), mutating-false-defaults-plan,\n  CreatedAt preservation\n\nPart of #189. Closes the settings.yaml pillar of #233.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Osorio Ortiz <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* feat(mecated): Phase 2b — schedules CLI subcommands (create/list/inspect/pause/resume/delete/fire)\n\nAdd 'mecated schedules <verb>' subcommands that dial the running server's\nHTTP API (/v1/schedules...). Follows the existing manual os.Args dispatch +\nstdlib flag pattern (peer of 'mecated config init' / 'mecated skills promote').\n\n- cmd/mecated/main.go: dispatchSubcommand refactor + 'schedules' dispatch\n- cmd/mecated/schedules_cmd.go: 7 verbs over the Phase 2a REST surface;\n  --server-addr, --output json|text; schedulePath helper (url.PathEscape)\n  + validateScheduleName guard (path-injection defense)\n- cmd/mecated/schedules_cmd_test.go: httptest-backed tests for all verbs,\n  body-shape assertions, missing-flag errors, invalid-name rejection,\n  JSON output, server-error propagation\n\nmecak8s deliberately omits CLI subcommands (parity with its existing policy);\nk8s users manage schedules via the gRPC/HTTP API.\n\nPart of #189. Closes the CLI management pillar of #233.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Osorio Ortiz <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* feat(scheduler): Phase 2b — schedule metrics (fires/skips/failures + fire latency)\n\nAdd schedule-fire metrics via a callback seam (Config.ScheduleMetrics), keeping\nthe scheduler package telemetry-import-free (mirrors EmitScheduleEvent). Composition\ncloses over telemetry.Metrics.EmitSchedule.\n\n- internal/adapter/telemetry/metrics.go: scheduleFires counter (outcome label:\n  fired/skipped/failed) + scheduleFireDuration histogram (in latencyInstruments\n  for explicit-bucket views) + EmitSchedule(payload, duration); nil-safe\n- internal/adapter/scheduler/scheduler.go: Config.ScheduleMetrics callback +\n  SetScheduleMetrics late-bind + emitScheduleMetrics chokepoint in fireClaimed\n  (fired/failed, time.Since(claim-now)) and fireOne/FireNow skip paths (duration=0);\n  extracted scheduleKindFired/Skipped/Failed constants\n- internal/app/build.go: ScheduleMetricsEmitter cfg field + wired in startScheduler\n- cmd/mecated + cmd/mecatui/embed: closure over metrics.EmitSchedule (mirrors\n  MetricsRoleScoper); mecak8s/mecatequi nil (byte-identical metrics-silent default)\n- Tests: scrape assertions + fired/failed/skipped callback invocation with\n  deterministic fake-clock durations\n\nSchedule metrics are NOT a role-family (no 'schedule' in roleFamily — fires mint\nfresh sessions whose own runs already carry role=main). The 'registered' polled\ngauge deferred (a separate observable-gauge seam; core scope covered).\n\nPart of #189. Closes the metrics pillar of #233.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Osorio Ortiz <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* docs(scheduler): Phase 2b — flip production-readiness to shipped + e2e declarative test\n\nUpdate living docs to reflect the three Phase 2b pillars (settings.yaml schedules:\nblock, mecated schedules CLI, schedule metrics) and add an end-to-end test through\napp.Build for the declarative → store path.\n\n- docs/design/PRODUCTION-READINESS.md: ⛔ Phase 2b → ✅ shipped\n- docs/design/IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md: Phase 2b subsection (config + CLI + metrics)\n- docs/usage.md: settings.yaml schedules syntax + CLI examples (shipped status)\n- docs/architecture.md: declarative config + CLI section\n- internal/app/schedules_declarative_test.go: e2e through app.Build — operator-tier\n  settings.yaml → foldOperatorSchedules → reconcileSchedules → store; idempotent\n  re-reconcile (no churn); project-tier schedules ignored (operator-tier-only)\n\nPart of #189. Closes #233.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Osorio Ortiz <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(scheduler): Phase 2b review fixes — protojson body decode, CLI mode/workspace, profile-aware workspace + singleton honesty\n\nAddresses the review findings on the Phase 2b schedules work (create path, CLI,\nmetrics, docs). A live end-to-end run against OpenRouter surfaced two of these.\n\n- H1 (server): decode the schedule create/update HTTP body with protojson into\n  *mecatlv1.ScheduleSpec (the shape the struct's own comment already claimed)\n  instead of a stdlib-json decode of a hand-rolled struct. The old path returned\n  HTTP 400 on ANY one-shot trigger (RFC3339 string vs *timestamppb.Timestamp).\n  Deletes the now-unused scheduleSpecBody + toProto. Regression test: one-shot\n  create round-trip.\n\n- CLI: add --mode and --workspace to `mecated schedules create` and default a\n  non-mutating schedule to plan mode (mirroring the declarative fold), so the\n  documented basic `create --cron ... --prompt ...` works instead of tripping the\n  server's non-mutating-must-be-plan invariant. --mode word -> protojson enum name.\n\n- NEW: validate the workspace PROFILE-AWARE at the schedule create-seam\n  (validateScheduleSpec), mirroring the session create-seam — a default-profile\n  schedule requires a workspace, a no-fs schedule must not carry one. Fail-closed:\n  previously an empty-workspace schedule was accepted at create but failed at FIRE\n  time (\"workspace is required\"), i.e. a schedule that could never fire. Test\n  fixtures updated; new TestCreateScheduleWorkspaceProfileInvariant.\n\n- M1 (honesty): foldOperatorSchedules WARNs when a declared singleton:false is\n  coerced to true (a bare bool cannot express the opt-out; deferred), and the docs\n  + the ScheduleDecl doc-comment (the configref source) state the v1 limitation.\n\n- L2 (CLI): validateScheduleName rejects bare \".\" / \"..\".\n- L3 (metrics): cover the singleton-overlap skip metric emit path.\n- N1/N2 (docs): CLI body-comment honesty; the fire duration is due->terminal, not\n  Claim->terminal (metrics.go + architecture / observability / impl-notes).\n\nVerified: task lint + task test green (root + engine + GOWORK=off standalone);\nmecademo full offline session; and a LIVE end-to-end run against OpenRouter\n(create -> force-fire -> real agent turn \"Hello from a scheduled task!\" ->\nstop=end_turn -> mecatl_schedule_fires_total{outcome=\"fired\"}).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jakub Hrozek <jakub@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
