          "id": "a1a7b542d0195e83cf147702e158bf192408aa8c",
          "message": "feat(server): add ForkSession — peer session from a history snapshot (#266)\n\n* feat(server): add ForkSession — peer session from a history snapshot\n\nAdds a ForkSession gRPC RPC + POST /v1/sessions/{id}/fork route that\nsnapshots a completed/idle session's conversation into a new equally-\ntrusted peer session, inheriting mode/workspace/limits/provider/model/\nprofile. Reuses the existing session.ForkSnapshot/SeedHistory primitives\nfrom the subagent fork path; same provider/model only. See ADR 0065.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): address review — add title override, save-first comment, ADR prose\n\nThree findings from the panel review on PR #266:\n\n1. DevEx should-fix: add an optional `title` field to ForkSessionRequest\n   (empty → inherit the source's title, non-empty → override). Without it a\n   forked session is indistinguishable from its source in ListSessions. This\n   is a v1-now-or-never addition to a published request message. Threaded\n   through the gRPC handler, the HTTP handler (optional JSON body), and the\n   Service.ForkSession signature. + test (TestForkSessionTitleOverride).\n\n2. Architecture Low: add a comment on the save-first-then-rehydrate ordering\n   noting the self-heal at StartRunContent (needsRehydration re-runs\n   rehydrateSession). Do NOT Store.Delete on failure — it would race a\n   concurrent rehydrating run.\n\n3. ADR prose nits: fix `&src.Conversation` → `src.Conversation` (Conversation\n   is *Conversation, so & would be **Conversation); fix \"source untouched\n   (read-only Load)\" → honest \"loadAndReopen may re-persist a terminal source\n   as a side effect, but its history is untouched\". Document the title field\n   in the wire-surface section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>",
