          "id": "795311c1210ef426f5382dbed67cacb10cfa4669",
          "message": "refactor(tools): graduate the six FS tool bodies into engine/adapter/fstools (#269) (#277)\n\n* refactor(tools): graduate the six FS tool bodies into engine/adapter/fstools (#269)\n\nMove the correctness/security-critical tool bodies — Read, Edit, Write,\nGrep, Glob, and the optional Bash — into the importable engine module as\nengine/adapter/fstools, so external consumers of engine/agent get them, and\nEdit's read-before-edit / exact-match / uniqueness invariants, by import\nrather than re-derivation. The bodies depend only on engine/session +\nengine/tool (+ the injected tool.Workspace/CommandRunner); the toolkit\ndependency in bash.go is replaced by locally-inlined MaxOutputBytes/\nTruncationMarker/truncate helpers.\n\nThe root internal/adapter/tools package re-exports the tool types, NewBashTool,\nand BashToolName via a thin alias shim (alias.go) and keeps the host-coupled\nweb/MCP tools (WebFetch, WebSearch, FetchMcpResource). tools.All()/NoFS()\npreserve the exact prior bundles and order, so every existing caller\n(internal/app, cmd/mecademo, server) compiles unchanged.\n\nTests: the FS-body behavior tests + argkeys drift-guard move into fstools\n(offline, memfs-only). The mixed FS+web catalog-shape tests stay in root.\nabspath_tools_test.go / read_readroots_test.go stay in root because they\nimport internal/adapter/osfs, which the engine module must not reach.\n\nAlso: engine-adapter-fstools strict depguard block; MaxOutputBytes lockstep\nmirror-comment in engine/session/content.go; COMPATIBILITY.md + AGENTS.md\nreference-adapter inventory updates.\n\nVerified: engine-standalone (GOWORK=off) build+test, api:check, root\ngo test ./..., docs:check, and mecademo offline session all pass. llms.txt\nregenerates byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(tools): address PR review — accurate output-cap docs, NewBashTool as a func\n\n- engine/session/content.go + engine/adapter/fstools/fstools.go: correct the\n  output-cap comments. MaxToolResultTextBytes (25 KiB = 25,600) is a domain-level\n  upper bound on ANY tool-result text block; the adapter caps\n  (fstools/toolkit.MaxOutputBytes = 25,000) sit strictly under it. Only those two\n  are byte-identical — the ~600-byte headroom to the domain bound is deliberate.\n  Drop the misleading \"keep the three in lockstep\" wording.\n- internal/adapter/tools/tools.go: clarify that WebSearch (like Bash) is NOT in\n  All()/NoFS() — it needs a search provider and is registered separately via\n  NewWebSearchTool(provider).\n- internal/adapter/tools/alias.go: re-export NewBashTool as a wrapper function\n  instead of a reassignable package var, so no other package can swap the\n  constructor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
