          "id": "bb706b23619195404089f08771b75db843e92670",
          "message": "fix(llmresilience): retry truncated/malformed streams and count them toward the breaker (#283)\n\nAn occasional \"agent: start stream: unexpected end of JSON input\" came from a\ntruncated first SSE frame: the openai-go ssestream decoder parses each frame with\nencoding/json, so a partial frame yields a *json.SyntaxError. (A transient 5xx with\nan empty gateway body can likewise hand back the raw json error, its status\ndiscarded by the SDK.) Neither DefaultClassifier nor isTransientForBreaker\nrecognised these, so they surfaced instead of retrying — and a persistent one would\nretry MaxAttempts every call without ever opening the shared breaker.\n\nTreat *json.SyntaxError and io.ErrUnexpectedEOF as a transient class in BOTH the\nretry classifier and the breaker predicate (kept in lockstep): at establishment a\ntruncated/malformed payload is a transient transport/proxy truncation, retryable\nand bounded by MaxAttempts + the shared breaker. Benefits every streaming provider.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
