          "id": "16f54c21eea19b83562b92d05fbede9547f14572",
          "message": "feat: optional auth.yaml credentials file for provider keys (#294)\n\n* feat(cliconfig): read provider credentials from an auth.yaml file\n\nAdds an optional settings.yaml-sibling credentials file\n(~/.config/mecatl/auth.yaml, providers.<name>.api_key) as a second source\nfor the four provider keys, so a key doesn't have to live in the shell's\nexported environment where any other process it spawns can read it. The\nenvironment always wins when both are present, so existing env-var-only\ndeployments are byte-identical. Kept as its own file (not a settings.yaml\nsubtree) so settings.yaml stays free of secrets and safe to share, and to\nleave room for OAuth token storage later without a schema break.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* review: extract authfile into an adapter package, fix panel-review findings\n\nPanel review (Spec/Standards clean; Domain: security, architecture, reuse,\nduplication) surfaced three real issues, addressed here:\n\n- Extract auth.yaml parsing into internal/adapter/authfile (a leaf adapter\n  mirroring xdgconfig's shape) so a future credential-writing subcommand can\n  depend on the schema without pulling in cliconfig's flag/model-alias\n  machinery (software-architect finding).\n- Fix a verified, reproducible secret leak: a YAML structural type mismatch\n  (e.g. forgetting the api_key: nesting) made the underlying decoder's error\n  echo a fragment of the real key into the warning/log path. Decode errors\n  are now reported generically, never with the library's raw error text\n  (secure-code-reviewer finding, CWE-532/OWASP A09).\n- Add a non-fatal permission warning when auth.yaml is group/other-readable\n  (secure-code-reviewer finding, CWE-522/732/A02).\n- Wire the same warning surfacing into cmd/mecak8s, a fourth consumer of\n  ProviderFlags.Apply missed in the first pass.\n\nAlso applied the reuse-review's mechanical simplifications (cmp.Or for the\nenv-wins-over-file merge, maps/slices for the unknown-provider filter).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(user-docs): note the auth.yaml alternative to env-var credentials\n\nTwo pages stated credentials come only from environment variables, which\npredates the auth.yaml file support added earlier in this branch. Minimal\nfix, linking out to the full docs/usage/mecated.md reference rather than\nduplicating the schema/precedence details here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* review: value-free unknown-provider warning, accumulate auth.yaml warnings\n\n- Unknown provider names now reported as a count, never verbatim: a\n  secret typed where the provider name belongs (inverted nesting) would\n  otherwise echo into operator logs (CWE-532 / OWASP A09).\n- The loose-permission warning is accumulated with content warnings\n  (joinWarnings) instead of clobbered by them — the security finding\n  survives a co-occurring typo.\n- Regression tests: secret-shaped provider name never leaks; combined\n  0644 + unknown-provider case asserts both warnings land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* chore: retrigger CI for PR #294\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
