          "id": "957335c55c16c6ef585a8f4b1608483e370857fc",
          "message": "feat(models): seamless model switch that always keeps the conversation (#20) (#295)\n\n* feat(models): same-provider context carryover on model switch (issue #20)\n\nThe /models picker restart-now flow starts a new session on the picked model\n(provider/model fixed per session => switching = new CreateSession), and until\nnow the transcript was always reset. Add an optional same-provider carryover:\nthe confirm overlay gains a [c] carry-over key that seeds the new session with\nthe current session's conversation, so a model switch can feel like a\ncontinuation rather than a cold start.\n\nWire: one additive proto field, CreateSessionRequest.source_session_id (8),\nserver-side so the service owns load/validate/seed and the same-provider gate.\n\nServer (internal/adapter/server):\n- validateCarryover loads the source via the run-entry funnel loadAndReopen,\n  rejects a running/awaiting source (FailedPrecondition), rejects a\n  cross-provider switch (InvalidArgument; provider canonicalised to the\n  default when empty; the MODEL is intentionally not compared — v1 carries the\n  conversation onto a different model within the same provider), and snapshots\n  via session.ForkSnapshot. seedCarryover seeds via SeedHistory before the\n  first Store.Save. Reuses the ADR-0065 fork primitives; zero engine/domain\n  change, port.LLMRequest untouched.\n- Threaded through the gRPC CreateSession handler and the HTTP POST\n  /v1/sessions handler.\n\nmecatui: [c] key gated on liveProviderID() == candidate provider (offered only\nfor a same-provider switch); restartOnModelWithCarryover + carryoverCmd mirror\nrestartOnModel, closing the old session best-effort after the new one is\nready; CreateSessionWithCarryover added to the client and the SessionCreator\ninterface (additive sibling).\n\nTurn-zero compaction needs no new code: maybeCompact already runs at every\nturn top against the new model's live-resolved window, with the recent user\ninstructions surviving via snapCutToRecentUserTurn.\n\nCross-provider carryover (strip Message.Reasoning/ProviderPhase) is deferred\nto v2 — v1 rejects it loudly rather than silently stripping.\n\nTests (offline, mockllm/memfs/teatest): service-level seed/same-provider/\nboth-default/running+awaiting/missing; gRPC + HTTP handler-wiring (mutation-\nverified: dropping the field-wiring line turns them red); turn-zero compaction\nthrough the real loop (recent user turn survives verbatim, history stays\ntool-pairing-valid); UI confirm-key unit + teatest e2e (handoff, cross-provider\nkey swallowed, failure recoverable); new models_confirm_carryover golden.\n\nDocs: IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES carryover section, PRODUCTION-READINESS flip,\nADR 0016 mid-session-switch note, ADR 0065 see-also, docs/tui.md [c] key,\nuser-docs gRPC/HTTP surface.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(models): seamless model switch that always keeps the conversation (#20)\n\nA model switch now keeps the conversation instead of restarting cold. Picking a\nmodel in the /models picker switches immediately — no confirm overlay, no\nfresh-vs-carry choice — and the new session is seeded from the current one.\n/clear remains the single explicit fresh-start verb.\n\nServer (internal/adapter/server): CreateSessionRequest.source_session_id\n(additive proto field 8) seeds a new session from a source via the existing\nsession.ForkSnapshot + SeedHistory primitives (zero engine-loop change).\nvalidateCarryover loads the source through the run-entry funnel loadAndReopen,\nrejects a running/awaiting source (FailedPrecondition), and seeds before the\nfirst Store.Save. Carryover is always allowed across providers:\n\n  - same provider  -> the snapshot replays VERBATIM (Reasoning/ProviderPhase/\n    ToolCall.ItemID intact, warm prompt-cache prefix);\n  - cross provider -> session.StripProviderState clears the provider-private\n    replay blobs, yielding a provider-neutral history both adapters omit\n    safely; the new session's thinking/reasoning config is derived from the\n    NEW model, not the stripped history.\n\nCross-provider onto OpenAI additionally synthesizes stable, deterministic,\nnon-fc_-prefixed ItemIDs (carryover_item_N) on the carried tool calls: the\nOpenAI store:false replay de-duplicates function_call items by the provider\nid, and an id-less carried item collides with auto-assigned fc_N on the second\nturn (Azure GPT-5.x \"Duplicate item\" 400). Anthropic ignores ItemID, so\nnon-OpenAI destinations stay bare-stripped.\n\nDomain (engine/session): new exported StripProviderState — a pure, non-mutating\ntransform clearing Message.Reasoning, Message.ProviderPhase, and every\nToolCall.ItemID while preserving roles/text/tool-call IDs/Args/tool results/\nparts. Classified Added (minor) per COMPATIBILITY.md; engine/api/session.txt\nregenerated.\n\nmecatui: the modelsConfirm overlay (enter/c/s/esc) is removed. chooseModel now\nroutes directly — a live session switches via restartOnModelWithCarryover\n(CreateSessionWithCarryover), no live session falls back to a plain create. A\none-shot status note names the switch (\"switched to <model> — conversation\nkept\"; cross-provider adds \"prior reasoning cache dropped\"). /clear is\nuntouched and documented as the fresh-start.\n\nTests (offline: mockllm/memfs/fakeConv/teatest): StripProviderState unit\n(all three blob fields, parts/tool-result preserved, no input mutation,\ntool-pairing-valid, backing-array isolation); service-level same-provider-\nverbatim vs cross-provider-strip vs OpenAI-synthesis (determinism pinned);\ngRPC + HTTP handler wiring incl. a cross-provider gRPC round-trip\n(mutation-verified); running/awaiting/missing-source rejection; turn-zero\ncompaction through the real loop; UI seamless-switch unit + teatest e2e\n(live-session carry, no-session plain create, cross-provider still carries,\nstatus-note wording, overlay removal leaves no dangling refs).\n\nDocs: IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES + PRODUCTION-READINESS updated, docs/tui.md /models\nrewritten, user-docs gRPC/HTTP surface, proto comment. ADR 0016 (which\ndocuments the removed overlay UX) is superseded by a follow-up ADR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs(adr): ADR 0071 — seamless model switch always keeps the conversation\n\nRecords the redesign that supersedes ADR 0016's mid-session-switch confirm\noverlay and same-provider carryover gate, and ADR 0065's same-provider\ncarryover constraint: a model switch always keeps the conversation (verbatim\nsame-provider, StripProviderState cross-provider, OpenAI ItemID synthesis).\nAdds the 'Superseded by' pointers on the two frozen ADRs (the only edit a\nfrozen ADR takes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
