          "id": "44d4b3a96164c2a63ebf3b51dcc345c99a2482d4",
          "message": "feat(process): converge the acceptance-plan spine + ac-trace into mecatl (#304)\n\n* feat(process): converge the acceptance-plan spine + ac-trace into mecatl\n\nBring the spine the sibling repos (the internal sibling repos) run into\nmecatl for a better multi-dev, agent-driven experience:\n\n- .claude/skills/to-acceptance-plan — design → docs/acceptance/<plan>.md\n  with numbered ACs + verify: lines (template + check script included)\n- .claude/skills/plan-orchestrate — decompose → parallel tdd-worker waves\n  → accumulator → aggregate gate → ac-trace --strict → inline panel-review\n  → one PR (never merges to main)\n- .claude/skills/test-writer — invariant-first test discipline adapted to\n  mecatl (offline mockllm/memfs + conformance suites, two modules)\n- .claude/skills/onboarding — the router mapping the spine + specialists\n- .claude/agents/tdd-worker + devils-advocate — the worker and the\n  pre-dispatch design critic, parameterized to mecatl's anchors\n- ac-trace wired as a Go tool (go.mod) + Taskfile ac-trace tasks\n  (report-only until a landed plan exists)\n- docs/development-process.md, docs/acceptance/README.md, and\n  docs/design/principles.md (the ac-trace grounding list)\n- docs/acceptance/spine-convergence.md — the dogfood plan for this change\n\npanel-review is unchanged — mecatl's version (default-on reuse pair:\ncode-duplication + library-reuse reviewers) is the converged one.\ndev-pipeline stays as the issue-scale track.\n\n* fix(process): panel-review follow-ups — principles drift-guard, ADR 0072, PR-only carve-out\n\n- principles.md: disclaim as a convenience index (canonical text in the\n  cited ADRs/AGENTS.md wins; update the summary with any invariant change)\n- ADR 0072 records the spine adoption (ADR 0002 rule 4: new design is a\n  new record) + the per-plan Status lifecycle's scope note\n- AGENTS.md Workflow: the spine's PR-only exception to commit-to-main\n\n* fix(process): invoke ac-trace via pinned go run, not a go.mod tool directive\n\nac-trace is an INTERNAL stacklok module. A go.mod tool directive put it in\nthe root module's build graph, so every CI build (which has no internal-org\nmodule access) failed resolving it. Invoke via go run …@v0.0.3 in the\nTaskfile tasks instead — same invocation mecatl already uses for matlatl /\nmodelith, and it keeps the module out of the build graph.",
