          "message": "fix(schedule): the Schedule tool on every schedule-capable session (ADR 0076) (#314)\n\n* docs(acceptance): schedule-shared-catalog plan + ADR 0076\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* refactor(schedule): move the schedule seam off *Service onto a store-shaped manager (ADR 0076)\n\nThe validated create/read/update/fire seam lived on *server.Service as methods\nreaching into s.cfg. It is in fact STORE-SHAPED — every input it needs (the\nScheduleStore type-asserted off the session store, a now-func, the cadence\nfloor, the event-log, diagnostics) is available before buildEngine. Move it\nverbatim onto a standalone scheduleManager (new schedule_manager.go),\nconstructed from the store + now-func alone, with the scheduler + model\ninventory as late-bound atomic fields. *Service keeps thin delegating\nwrappers so the RPC surface (grpc_schedule.go, REST /v1/schedules, the mecatui\n/schedule overlay) is byte-identical.\n\nComposition (app.Build) constructs the manager from the store BEFORE buildEngine\nand hands it to server.Config.ScheduleManager; the Service adopts it and\nlate-binds its models pointer so SetModels keeps working with no second copy.\nassets.scheduleManagerFactory is still bound LATE (after NewService) — the\neager binding is task 02. This is a pure refactor: zero behaviour change.\n\nPins AC1.1/AC1.3/AC1.4 of the schedule-shared-catalog plan:\n- TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario1_ManagerIsStoreShaped (AC1.1)\n- TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario1_ServiceDelegates (AC1.3)\n- TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario1_FireNowStatesPreserved (AC1.4)\n\nAll existing schedule tests stay green (schedule_test.go, schedule_e2e_test.go,\nschedule_validation_test.go, schedule_wire_survives_test.go, internal/app\nscheduletool tests, TestPerSessionCatalogMatchesSharedCatalog).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(schedule): eager factory bind — the shared catalog carries Schedule/ScheduleQuery (ADR 0076, task 02)\n\nbuildEngine now constructs the store-shaped schedule manager from the\nsession store BEFORE any catalog assembly and buildCatalog binds\nassets.scheduleManagerFactory onto the assets before the build-time\nassembleCatalog pass — so registerScheduleTool fires on the SHARED pass\nand the build-time shared catalog gains Schedule (mutating) +\nScheduleQuery (read-only), exactly like the six memory tools (ADR 0073\ndecision 1). The late bind (assets.scheduleManagerFactory =\nsvc.ScheduleManager after server.NewService) and the stale\n\"chicken-and-egg / legitimately has no Schedule tool\" comments are\ndeleted: sessionNeedsPerFactory has no schedule arm, so the\ndefault-profile shared-engine fast path (the plain mecatui launch) was\nschedule-less.\n\nBuild hands the SAME manager buildEngine returns to server.NewService\nvia server.Config.ScheduleManager (one manager, one truth). The manager\ncrosses composition as the concrete *scheduleManager (the new\nserver.ScheduleManagerImpl alias) with an explicit nil check in the\nfactory — a typed-nil interface would defeat registerScheduleTool's\nmgr == nil honest-absence gate and nil-panic NewService's\nsetModelsPointer adoption (caught by the full suite). A store with no\nScheduleStore keeps the tool honestly absent from BOTH catalogs (never\na stub).\n\nTestPerSessionCatalogMatchesSharedCatalog now covers the schedule pair\nwith NO carve-out: the pair joins requiredFamilyTools, fullyLoadedCfg\nbacks a ScheduleStore (StoreDir), and the drift guard passes the same\neager factory buildEngine performs. registerScheduleTool and\nscheduleManagerPresent are unchanged (they already no-op on a nil\nfactory/manager).\n\nAlso adds Config.MockProvider (test-only): a scripted provider seam\nthrough a full app.Build — UseMock scripts one fixed text turn and can\nnever emit a tool call, which the AC2.1 pin needs.\n\nverify:\n- AC2.1: TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario2_SharedCatalogHasScheduleTools\n  (store-backed Build; scripted Schedule + ScheduleQuery calls through a\n  default-profile shared-engine session; oracle = the run's own\n  EvToolResult — an unregistered tool comes back \"unknown tool\"; watched\n  red before the fix and red again with the eager bind planted out)\n- AC2.2: TestScheduleTool_RegisteredOnlyWhenStoreBacked (green)\n- AC2.3: TestPerSessionCatalogMatchesSharedCatalog (green, schedule pair\n  in requiredFamilyTools, no carve-out)\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(schedule): shared-engine posture note + default-session e2e (ADR 0070/0075, task 03)\n\nThe shared engine's Deps never got applySchedulePosture — today applied\nonly in the per-session factory (sessionEngineFactory) — so a\ndefault-profile, zero-selector session (the shared-engine fast path a\nplain mecatui launch takes) carried the Schedule tool in its catalog\n(task 02) but was never TOLD the tool exists (the ADR-0070 affordance\ngate). buildEngine now applies applySchedulePosture to the shared\nengine's PromptConfig under the SAME scheduleManagerPresent(assets) gate\nthe factory uses, mirroring the note's registration exactly (a store\nwith no ScheduleStore withholds it).\n\nFour Scenario-3 pins prove the end-to-end over a store-backed Build\n(launch-root workspace → the shared-engine fast path):\n\n- AC3.1: TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario3_DefaultSessionHasTool — the\n  shared engine's catalog resolves Schedule + ScheduleQuery (scripted\n  dispatch executes both, no unknown-tool error).\n- AC3.2: TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario3_SystemPromptCarriesScheduleNote\n  — the shared engine's system prompt carries schedulePostureNote on the\n  Role/StablePrefix layer (asserted against req.System.StablePrefix, not\n  the combined Render); watched RED before the fix (launch-root session\n  → shared engine), GREEN after; a store-less shared engine withholds it.\n- AC3.3: TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario3_OriginAndDeliveryWired — a\n  schedule created from a shared-engine session stamps OriginSessionID\n  (OriginBinder live), and the production fire path (scheduler.FireNow →\n  makeFireFunc → fireClaimed → deliverFireResult) enqueues the fire's\n  fenced result into the FileDeliveryQueue the shared engine's Step 2a\n  drain records into the origin chat (ADR 0075).\n- AC3.4: TestScheduleSharedCatalog_Scenario3_RehydratedSessionKeepsTool —\n  a default-profile session persisted then reloaded (a second Build over\n  the SAME store, the restart path) still resolves the Schedule tool on\n  the restored shared engine.\n\nThe tests create sessions on the LAUNCH-ROOT workspace so\nsessionNeedsPerFactory is false (the shared-engine fast path); an early\ndraft passed a t.TempDir() workspace and silently exercised the\nper-session factory, masking the missing shared-engine wiring — caught\nby watching AC3.2 fail against the launch-root session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs(acceptance): flip schedule-shared-catalog plan to landed\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* chore(plan): schedule-shared-catalog task ledger\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
