          "id": "d9642d51fdbe177788a2da402aa4280880fb97bf",
          "message": "feat: factory MCP wiring — --mcp-server on mecatequi/mecak8s + compact summary (#341) (#347)\n\nRegister the repeatable --mcp-server name=URL flag and the MCP_<NAME>_TOKEN\nbearer convention on mecatequi and mecak8s via a shared cliconfig.MCPServerList\nhelper (extracted from mecated, which now uses it too), so a scheduler\n(titlani) can inject a short-lived per-run identity the run presents to vmcp /\ntequitl MCP endpoints. An EXPLICIT --out-summary=- on mecatequi now selects a\nstdout-compact mode: the Summary is emitted as a single compact JSON line as the\nFINAL stdout line (the unset default keeps indented JSON). --run-id/--task-ref\nare deliberately NOT accepted — schedulers correlate via their own launch\nidentity plus Summary.session_id.\n\nSecurity-review hardenings (deliberately tightening mecated too):\n- CWE-178: server names must match [A-Za-z0-9_]+ and be case-insensitively\n  unique (vmcp/VMCP/vMcp all derive MCP_VMCP_TOKEN; my-svc would derive an\n  unsettable env var and silently connect unauthenticated).\n- CWE-319: a token-bearing URL must be https, or http to loopback (reuses\n  mcp.ValidateClientURL), so an injected bearer never travels cleartext\n  off-host. Tokenless URLs are not gated.\nDocs note that on mecak8s the token is read once at startup and shared\nprocess-wide (per-run identity is mecatequi-only; per-session credentials are\nmecatl#342), and that the compact-summary last-line guarantee is stdout-only —\na merged pod log consumer must take the last line that PARSES as the Summary.\n\nRecorded as ADR 0082 (pairs with titlani's run-contract ADR 0010); factory\ninvocation profile documented in docs/usage/mecatequi-ci.md. cmd/internal layer\nonly — the engine module and its API surface are untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
