          "message": "feat(telemetry): opt-in telemetry for headless binaries (mecatequi, mecak8s) (#343) (#393)\n\n* feat(telemetry): opt-in telemetry for headless binaries (mecatequi, mecak8s) (#343)\n\nThe headless mains deliberately wired Sink/ToolCallRecorder/metrics to nil,\nleaving a factory running many one-shot invocations with no fleet-level\ntelemetry beyond exit codes and JSONL event files. Reuse the existing\ninternal/adapter/telemetry pipeline (the SAME Setup + NewMetrics +\nWithRole role-scoper path mecated uses) behind opt-in, default-off flags\nso the no-telemetry posture stays byte-identical.\n\n- internal/adapter/telemetry: add an optional OTLP METRICS push reader\n  (PeriodicReader over otlpmetricgrpc/http) alongside the always-on\n  prometheus reader, gated on new OTLPConfig.Metrics* fields. Existing\n  scrape-only callers are untouched.\n- mecatequi (short-lived one-shot, scrape does not fit): opt-in\n  --otlp-* / --otlp-metrics-* push flags with an explicit flush-before-exit\n  bounded by --otlp-shutdown-timeout so a dead collector can't hang CI.\n- mecak8s (long-lived server, scrape fits): opt-in --metrics-addr loopback\n  /metrics listener (non-loopback rejected fail-closed per ADR 0018) plus\n  opt-in OTLP push twin for non-scrape deployments.\n- internal/cliconfig: shared HeadlessTelemetry helper (Rule of Three across\n  the two new mains) + a canonical IsLoopbackAddr replacing the duplicated\n  loopback checks in mecated and mecak8s.\n- Reuses the existing mecatl.* instruments (no new metrics); per-run token\n  counters ride EvResult.Usage. Labels stay the issue-#47 closed Role set.\n  Cost counter deferred to #192 (pricing deliberately unparsed).\n- ADR 0097 + ADR 0027 List-1 inventory rows + usage/user-docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* test(mecak8s): run TestTelemetryMetricsAddrServesPrometheus on the mock provider\n\nThe scrape e2e called app.Build without --mock, so it depended on a real\nprovider key in the environment. It passed locally (a key was present) but\nfailed in CI with \"no LLM provider available\". Pin it to --mock like the\nsibling telemetry tests so it is hermetic and offline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>",
