          "id": "6addc98cfedf2e8033832878c01cbccb0c5e9574",
          "message": "feat(driver): remote schedule registry via ScheduleStoreService driver protocol (#257) (#404)\n\n* feat(driver): ScheduleStoreService + ScheduleOneShotReArmerService driver protocol (#257)\n\nAdd the remote schedule-registry seam to the driver protocol so a\ndeployment can run its schedule store in a separate driver process,\nconsistent with SessionStoreService/EventLogService/SessionLeaseService.\n\n- contracts/proto/mecatl/driver/v1/schedule_store.proto: the 13-RPC\n  ScheduleStoreService (Save/Load/Delete/List/Due/Claim/ClaimNow/\n  SetEnabled/RecordFire/RecordFireStart/RecordFireProgress/LoadFire/\n  ListFires) + the 1-RPC ScheduleOneShotReArmerService (ReArmOneShot).\n  Schedules and fires cross as opaque format-tagged JSON envelopes\n  (schedule-json/1) the driver round-trips verbatim; the atomic\n  Claim/ClaimNow/ReArmOneShot advance is implemented server-side by the\n  driver (the harness client cannot fence over the wire) — the same\n  trusted-peer posture SessionStoreService takes for snapshot opacity.\n- internal/adapter/grpcdriver/schedulestore.go: the thin client wrapper\n  (port.ScheduleStore + port.ScheduleOneShotReArmer over the wire;\n  NOT_FOUND -> ErrScheduleNotFound, UNIMPLEMENTED -> ErrScheduleUnsupported,\n  mis-keyed-driver and unknown-format guards) + the fail-closed server\n  wrappers (every RPC validates before touching the backend; top-level\n  key vs decoded-payload mismatch is INVALID_ARGUMENT).\n- Validated by scheduleconformance.Run over bufconn (client -> wire ->\n  server wrapper -> memschedulestore), incl. the Claim/ClaimNow/ReArmOneShot\n  atomicity and RecordFire idempotency subtests, plus 20 wrapper unit\n  tests covering the error-classification and validation arms.\n\n* feat(mecated): --schedule-store-url override wiring the remote schedule registry (#257)\n\nCompose the wave-1 driver into the deployment: a dedicated, independent\n--schedule-store-url flag (the --event-log-url precedent; ADR 0059\ndecision #5's 'an independent override wins' arm) pointing the durable\nschedule registry at a remote ScheduleStoreService driver.\n\n- internal/app/build.go: resolveScheduleStore is the ONE resolution the\n  scheduler tick loop (buildScheduler), the fire path (startScheduler's\n  fireStore), and the delivery-queue gate (buildDeliveryQueue) all\n  share; the override dials through the shared driverConns cache\n  (equal URLs share one connection, once-guarded close) and fails loud\n  on dial error (an explicitly-configured driver that won't dial is an\n  operator misconfiguration, never a silent no-scheduling degrade).\n  Unset keeps the byte-identical store-accessor discovery.\n- cmd/mecated: the operator-tier flag + ACP-common-help exclusion\n  (server-boundary surface, never a project-tier knob).\n- Docs: PRODUCTION-READINESS flips the driver ScheduleStoreService from\n  deferred to shipped; architecture.md/observability.md/usage +\n  user-docs gain the flag and the two-service driver surface.\n\n* feat(server): ScheduleManagerConfig.ScheduleStore override — one registry for tool + tick loop (#257)\n\nClose the split-brain the wave-2 override would otherwise open: the\nin-chat Schedule tool's manager discovered its store ONLY by\ntype-asserting the session store, so --schedule-store-url + an\naccessor-less session store left the tool absent while the tick loop\nran remote (and with an accessor-ful store the two would manage\nDIFFERENT registries).\n\nScheduleManagerConfig gains an OPTIONAL explicit ScheduleStore that\nwins over the accessor discovery (composition passes the one\nresolveScheduleStore result); nil keeps the byte-identical accessor\npath, and nil-from-both keeps the honest absent-manager semantics.\nPinned by the override tests (override shadows an accessor-ful store;\nbyte-identical arms unchanged) and the composition-level\nTestBuild_ScheduleStoreOverrideWiresScheduleTool /\nTestBuild_ScheduleStoreOverrideStartsScheduler.",
