          "message": "docs: regenerate stale llms.txt (drift from PR #418) (#428)\n\n* docs: handover for stale llms.txt (CI Docs/matlatl failing on main)\n\nThe Docs (matlatl) CI check fails on main's own tip, unrelated to any\nsingle PR: PR #418 (invalid-utf8) edited docs/design/IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md\nacross several commits without regenerating llms.txt (the AGENTS.md\n\"changed any Markdown -> task generate\" rule). Diagnosed but not fixed\nhere: this sandbox has no network egress to resolve the matlatl Go\nmodule, so the actual regen + commit needs a network-connected\nenvironment. See the handover doc for root cause and the exact fix\ncommand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate stale llms.txt, drop the handover doc\n\nThe prior sandbox couldn't resolve the matlatl Go module (no network\negress); this environment does, so the fix from the handover doc lands\nhere directly instead of waiting on a separate follow-up. Regenerated\nvia `task docs:llms` (drift was PR #418 editing\ndocs/design/IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md without a llms.txt regen).\nMatches this repo's own convention (see the deleted\nHANDOVER-reasoning-item-id-replay.md precedent): the handover doc is\nremoved once its fix lands in the same effort.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
