          "id": "45bfd77803d460526945aba84e6ede402e3f60f9",
          "message": "docs+fix(mecatui): document keymap overrides, live help-overlay bindings, isolate user-config test reads (#460)\n\n* docs+fix(mecatui): document keymap overrides; make ? overlay + welcome card read live bindings\n\nThe operator keybinding-override feature (keymap: in settings.yaml + the\n--keymap flag, validator in cmd/mecatui/keymap) existed but was documented\nnowhere, and the \"?\" help overlay rendered most chords as hardcoded literals\nthat would lie after a remap.\n\n- help.go: build a helpKeys markings struct once on the Model\n  (helpKeyMarkings/keyMarkings/firstKey) and thread it through\n  helpBody/renderHelpOverlay, so every rebindable row (Submit, Newline, Paste,\n  Cancel, MCPPanel, Resources, Prompts, Agents, Effort, ModeSwitch,\n  ExpandTools, Help, Quit, the scroll pair, and the close hint) reads the live\n  binding. The scroll row keeps the platform-adaptive marking while ScrollU/\n  ScrollD hold their defaults and switches to the remapped chords once rebound.\n  The welcome card (zeroStateRows) reads live too. Default rendering is\n  byte-identical (goldens unchanged).\n- help_test.go: TestHelpReflectsKeyOverride asserts all rebindable rows +\n  the close hint lead with their overridden chord; TestHelpKeyOverrideEndToEnd\n  wires Deps.KeyOverrides through New()→View(); TestKeyMarkingsEmptyBinding-\n  FallsBack pins the firstKey fallback.\n- docs/tui.md: new \"Remapping keys\" reference — the full action table with\n  scope, the textarea's own (non-rebindable) editing keys, both override\n  surfaces (CLI wins per action), and the validation rules.\n- user-docs/what-you-get/mecatui.md: a \"Remapping keys\" section with the\n  ctrl+a/ctrl+e → line-start/line-end worked example.\n\nIssue #455. Live reload (#456) and footer/inline-card liveness (#457) are\nseparate follow-ups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* test(app): isolate conventional user-config reads from the developer's real ~/.config\n\nThree internal/app tests failed on a developer machine whose real\n~/.config/mecatl/settings.yaml carries operator settings (posture: auto,\nBash(task lint:*) allows): the conventional user-global settings.yaml read\n(xdgconfig.OSEnv) leaked into the test's permission/posture fold.\n\n- TestBuildOperatorYAMLPostureSeam/project_tier_posture_is_ignored: the real\n  user-global posture: auto overrode the expected strict default.\n- TestResolveTrustMonotonicPositiveDenyHonoured + ...Remembered...: the real\n  user-global Bash allow rules surfaced as a ScopeCLI allow, tripping the\n  \"trust must not turn a project DENY into an ALLOW\" assertion.\n\nThe trust tests isolate the *trust* read via the trustEnv seam but build\npermconfig.New{Conventional:true} with no env, which independently reads the\nreal user-global file via xdgconfig.OSEnv (resolve.go). Add an\nisolateUserConfig(t) helper (t.Setenv XDG_CONFIG_HOME + HOME to empty temp\ndirs, the existing fakeUserConfigEnv idiom) and call it in the three tests.\nVerified load-bearing: removing the isolation re-fails the posture subtest\nagainst the real file.\n\nSigned-off-by: Joe Beda <joe@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-11T16:23:33-07:00",
