          "id": "77bb72d6030b07d39be79167486d481afbcceaff",
          "message": "feat(toolhive): direct mode via in-process OIDC token source (#265) (#453)\n\nmecatl imports ToolHive as a Go library and builds an in-process OIDC token source (llm.NewTokenSource) so the toolhive provider talks directly to the real gateway_url — no local proxy hop, no subprocess credential helper.\n\n- internal/adapter/toolhivellm/tokensource.go: the package's single ToolHive-importing file; non-interactive token source + RunInteractiveLogin + OIDCConfigured. Token never logged/env/error (llm.SanitizeTokenError); only the refresh-token reference persisted.\n- internal/app/registry.go: resolveToolhiveIntent discriminates proxy/direct; newDirectGatewayEntry injects the bearer per-request via a RoundTripper over openai.WithHTTPClient (survives per-session remint); HTTPS-scheme gate on gateway_url (host-compared, fail-closed); base URL = gateway_url + /v1.\n- --toolhive-llm-mode auto|proxy|direct (default auto) across all four mains.\n- mecatui login subcommand (interactive OIDC, SIGINT-aware).\n- Docs: ADR 0102, IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES, architecture/providers, usage.md, AGENTS.md, user-docs, ADR 0027 resource inventory (rows 39-40), regenerated llms.txt.\n- toolhive bumped v0.31.0 -> v0.40.0 (earliest with pkg/llm.NewTokenSource; avoids the mcpsdk v1.7.0 goroutine leak).\n\nCloses #265",
