          "id": "5aa468368647431d331c1796621933d1a166df99",
          "message": "docs: bump matlatl to v0.0.8 and enable respectGitignore (#479)\n\nmatlatl v0.0.8 adds opt-in --respect-gitignore (ADR 0024), which unions the\nrepo's effective git ignore set (tracked + nested .gitignore, .git/info/exclude,\nglobal excludes) with .matlatlignore. Enable it via .matlatl.yml\n(respectGitignore: true) so both the Taskfile and the CI action pick it up from\none place.\n\nThis fixes the local-vs-CI divergence where gitignored working files\n(HANDOFF.md, CLAUDE.local.md, agent scratch notes) were scanned as corpus\ndocuments: they no longer fail `matlatl check --strict` locally, and\nregenerating llms.txt no longer bakes a nonzero orphan count that breaks CI's\nclean-checkout staleness gate.\n\nBump the three pins from v0.0.7 to v0.0.8: the two Taskfile go-run invocations\n(docs:llms, docs:check) and the CI composite action SHA.\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
