          "id": "faa9730a6ddf635f8439a2bce978b66ba63db72f",
          "message": "feat(mecatui): split client keymap settings into ~/.config/mecatui/settings.yaml (#481)\n\nIssue #459: mecatui and mecated shared one operator settings file\n(~/.config/mecatl/settings.yaml) whose schema is server-owned and parsed\nstrictly, while mecatui read its single keymap: key out of the same file via\na separate lenient decoder the server silently dropped — the early \"git\nregret model\" (one config namespace read by two binaries, scope invisible\nfrom the file).\n\nGive mecatui its own client-owned settings file at\n~/.config/mecatui/settings.yaml (the XDG config tree, matching the existing\nmecatui/themes dir). v1 moves only keymap: — the one key with an existing\ndecoder and users (#455/#460/#467); the strict top-level clientSettings\nschema is designed to grow additive fields (theme, UI behaviour) as small\nfollow-ups without re-designing.\n\n- New file parses STRICTLY (yaml.NewDecoder + KnownFields(true), the\n  daemonconfig idiom): an unknown top-level key or a multi-document file is\n  a startup error naming the file; raw YAML syntax errors are not wrapped\n  through (CWE-209 — they embed the offending source line).\n- The legacy server file stays LENIENT (plain Unmarshal tolerates the\n  server's permissions:/guardrails:/models: siblings) for back-compat: an\n  operator's existing keymap: keeps working.\n- Precedence, per action (a higher layer rebinds only the actions it\n  names): CLI --keymap > client file > legacy server file. No env form for\n  keymap exists, so the chain is three layers.\n- A legacy keymap: fires a one-line stderr deprecation WARN at startup\n  (pre-alt-screen, direct write not slog) pointing at the new home.\n- The legacy parser now applies the same TypeError-vs-syntax split as the\n  strict reader so a wrong-typed keymap: value no longer leaks a truncated\n  slice of the offending value into the returned error (CWE-209; flagged by\n  the panel's security axis and pinned by a regression test).\n\nDocs: docs/tui.md \"Remapping keys\" and user-docs/what-you-get/mecatui.md\nnow name the client file as primary, document the three-layer precedence,\nand note the legacy deprecation. Server-scoped docs/configuration-reference.md\nand the configgen skeleton are untouched (the server schema is unchanged;\nconfigref regen is a no-op). llms.txt regen is a no-op (index only).\n\nDeferred (out of scope, per the issue): theme/UI-flag/env-knob settings\nlayer, a client configgen reference generator (until a second key lands),\na MECATUI_KEYMAP env form, the typed client->server spawn payload, and #456\nlive-reload.\n\nVerification: task lint (0 issues), task test (full suite, -race), go run\n./cmd/mecademo (full offline session), task site:build, task docs:check (0\nbroken links). 14 new offline tests cover path resolution, strict/lenient\ndecode, precedence, per-action merge, legacy-only back-compat (merged map\nequals the pre-split two-layer output), the deprecation WARN firing exactly\nonce, and the CWE-209 no-leak regression.\n\nCloses #459\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
