          "id": "1ec8f50e740be280ceca689ce531c4d0bcb47923",
          "message": "fix(deps): re-tidy root module after independent provider SDK bumps\n\nPR #381 and #383 bumped openai-go (v3.37.0->v3.50.0) and anthropic-sdk-go\n(v1.47.0->v1.62.0) inside provider/ssefilter's and provider/anthropic's own\ngo.mod, per dependabot's per-directory PR scope. Neither PR ran the root\n`task tidy` chain (root tidy -> go work sync -> per-module GOWORK=off tidy),\nso root go.mod/go.sum were left requiring the OLD versions directly/indirectly\neven though go.work's MVS already resolved the newer ones for actual builds.\n\nThis surfaced as a real CI failure on PR #477 (unrelated GitHub Actions bump,\nrebased onto main after #381/#383 landed): `ko resolve` failed on\n./cmd/mecated with \"go: updates to go.mod needed, disabled by -mod=readonly\"\nin the k8s-e2e job, because ko's own package-loading path needs a fully\nconsistent module graph under -mod=readonly that root's stale go.mod no\nlonger provided — while other jobs happened not to exercise the same path.\n\nFix: run `task tidy` at the root. Bumps root's go.mod to the same versions\nalready in effect via go.work's MVS, plus the transitive tidwall/gjson bump\nand a gopkg.in/yaml.v3 require-block move both submodules already picked up.\n\nVerified: go build ./... clean under GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly, task api:check\ngreen, task test:provider-standalone green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
