          "id": "1b443a2eb880b17fa1297099cc05bed082c46e05",
          "message": "feat(mecatui): ctrl+z suspend + ctrl+d double-press quit (#513)\n\n* feat(mecatui): ctrl+z suspend + ctrl+d double-press quit\n\nAdds two terminal-lifecycle keybindings (issue #504):\n\n- ctrl+z suspends the TUI to the shell (Bubble Tea tea.Suspend) in EVERY\n  state — idle, mid-run, the permission modal. A one-line stderr notice\n  (\"the mecatl engine is still running\") is written before suspending,\n  since the embedded mecated + any in-flight run KEEP RUNNING while the\n  UI is stopped; ResumeMsg re-syncs on fg.\n- ctrl+d is the unix EOF-habit quit: a SECOND graceful double-press\n  guard (arm → hint → timed disarm → second press quits), INDEPENDENT of\n  ctrl+c — neither key confirms the other, and validator rule 6 forbids\n  them sharing a chord. It fires only on an EMPTY prompt; on a populated\n  prompt the chord stays the textarea's DeleteCharacterForward.\n\nBoth are rebindable global keymap actions (Suspend / QuitD), documented\nin docs/tui.md + user-docs, with unit tests for arm/confirm/disarm,\nguard independence, the empty-prompt gate, and the every-phase suspend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(mecatui): surface ctrl+z/ctrl+d in the help overlay\n\nThe standards review of f4b0538f noted the new Suspend/QuitD actions had\nno helpKeys markings, so the '?' overlay never advertised them. Add\nsuspend/quitD markings (live-chord, honest under a remap) and two rows\nto the General section, regenerating the two help goldens (only the new\nrows change). Also fix a stray word in the docs/tui.md ctrl+d row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(mecatui): show the suspend notice on resume, not before suspend\n\nThe pre-suspend stderr notice landed in the alt-screen buffer (direct\nwrite) — discarded when the alt screen exits on suspend — or was frozen\nbefore Bubble Tea flushed its deferred-print queue (tea.Println has no\nflush tick before SIGTSTP). Neither path could survive to the shell, so\nthe notice never reached the operator's scrollback (jbeda's mosh/ssh/tmux\nreport made it visible; it reproduced in a clean pty too).\n\nFix: record the phase + session id at suspend, and emit the notice as an\nin-conversation notice on RESUME (tea.ResumeMsg) — the only moment the\noperator can read it. The notice names the session and what was\nsuspended (idle / a running turn / a pending ask / a replay) so a\nmid-run suspend's continuation is explicit, not surprising.\n\nDocs updated to describe the resume notice rather than a pre-suspend\nstderr line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
