          "id": "aac96eb6da1201d7a05d05a3498f070194e99321",
          "message": "feat(mecak8s): add file-based ci/ values fixtures to deploy:check (#671)\n\nAdds deploy/helm/mecak8s/ci/{production,production-oidc}-values.yaml and\nrenders both (helm template -f | kubeconform) inside task deploy:check,\nalongside the existing --set-based PROD_SET/OIDC_SET checks — a\ndiscoverable, `-f`-based example of a full production install, and the\nsame fixture-directory convention ToolHive's charts use for `ct lint`.\n\nDeliberately does NOT adopt the `ct` (chart-testing) binary: it shells\nout to Python yamale/yamllint even with its other validations disabled,\na real toolchain dependency this repo's otherwise-all-Go chain\n(kind/ko/kubeconform/kustomize) doesn't carry, for coverage `helm\ntemplate`+kubeconform already provide. Also confirmed `helm lint` alone\nwould have been the wrong tool for this regardless of `ct`: it does not\nfail on a template execution error (a `fail`/`required` violation\nprints as an INFO line and still exits 0), so it wouldn't catch the\nclass of error this exists to catch.\n\nAlso fixes a real, pre-existing bug in deploy:check found while testing\nthis: every `helm template | kubeconform` (and `| grep`) pipe in the\ntask ran under `set -eu` without `pipefail`, so a `helm template`\nfailure produced empty stdin for the next command in the pipe, which\nthen exited 0 — silently passing the task even though the chart failed\nto render at all. Added `-o pipefail` to every cmd block in the task.\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
