          "message": "fix: wait on the watchdog marker itself, not a self-referencing baseline (#684) (#685)\n\nTestStreamIdleDisabledSpawnsNoWatchdogGoroutine's settle step compared\nruntime.NumGoroutine() against a baseline sampled at the same call — a\nstill-unwinding watchdog goroutine from a prior test was already baked\ninto that baseline, so the check passed without ever waiting for it to\nexit, occasionally letting a stray restSeqIdleBounded frame land in the\n\"disabled\" sample. Poll the actual witness instead.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
