          "id": "9439e62c696c0a8e654d86b2a74a5cca2577c83d",
          "message": "fix(governance): accept-edits mode now auto-allows Edit/Write (#675)\n\nsession.ModeAccept (\"accept-edits\") was never consulted by\npermpolicy.Policy.Evaluate -- only session.ModePlan was, so a session in\naccept-edits mode was asked for permission on every Edit/Write call exactly\nas if it were in default mode, and even an \"allow always\" verdict only\npersisted a narrow exact-args pattern rather than a per-tool grant.\n\nEvaluate now folds a floor-loosening Edit/Write Allow (ScopeCLI, mirroring\nthe --yolo allow-all rule's scope) into the extra rule set under\nModeAccept, so it can only ever loosen the built-in mutate-ask floor and\nnever suppress a configured deny/ask. Bash is untouched.\n\nFixes #674.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
