          "id": "9fc6b416e8c0a7f6910dcf35866e9b9d77e78ad9",
          "message": "feat(providers): auto-detect the ToolHive LLM gateway proxy as a native provider (#263)\n\n* feat(providers): auto-detect the ToolHive LLM gateway proxy as a native provider\n\nWhen ToolHive's llm proxy (thv llm proxy start) is configured on the\nmachine, mecatl now registers a `toolhive` provider automatically and the\ngateway's per-credential-filtered models appear in the TUI picker — zero\nconfig, no API key. The org gateway is trusted, user-chosen infra; the\nrouting is disclosed continuously via a persistent \"via ToolHive gateway\"\nheader segment, startup diagnostics, and /models provider-status rows.\n\nTwo-layer design (ADR 0064), engine untouched:\n- internal/adapter/openaicompat: generic hardened vanilla /v1/models\n  lister (stdlib-only; size/rune caps, C0+C1 control-strip at the leaf,\n  redirect-refusing default client, errors.As-able StatusError).\n- internal/adapter/toolhivellm: the ONLY ToolHive-aware code — a\n  fail-soft, uid-ownership-gated, size-capped typed read of\n  ~/.config/toolhive/config.yaml's llm: block; never imports ToolHive Go\n  packages; never reads tls_skip_verify; base URL hardcoded to\n  http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1.\n- Composition: register-on-intent (probe never gates registration, so a\n  persisted toolhive session rehydrates into a request-time-failing\n  provider instead of a brick, and a late-started proxy heals on the next\n  /models open); explicit intent-driven-lowest default tier; bounded\n  1.5s Build probe drives diagnostics/default-model/status only;\n  last-known-good model snapshot for catalog-less providers; loopback-only\n  --toolhive-llm-base-url validation (CWE-918); reasoning-effort clamp.\n- Wire: additive ListModelsResponse.provider_status (string-state\n  discipline) rendered by mecatui as actionable /models remediation rows.\n- Flags via cliconfig on all four mains: --toolhive-llm (default true),\n  --toolhive-llm-base-url (no env twin).\n- newOpenAIEntry renamed newOpenAICompatEntry (it serves openai,\n  openrouter, and gateways).\n\nPanel-reviewed (spec/standards/security/architecture/duplication/reuse/\ndevex/ux/QA); all must-fix findings addressed, guard tests\nmutation-verified (defaultModel race, tier precedence, secret-field pin).\n\nDocs: ADR 0064, usage walkthrough + troubleshooting, architecture\nproviders section, ADR-0027 inventory rows, IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.\n\nCloses #262\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KboCzrvXKCLEpfhgzB7SGf\n\n* fix(providers): address PR #263 review findings — heal reach, refresh race, inference redirects\n\nReview-feedback round (rdimitrov's 8 findings + 3 cleanups, panel-re-reviewed):\n\n- F1: a healed default model now reaches zero-selector sessions — the\n  pending-default posture (server.Config.DefaultModelPending) routes them\n  through the per-session factory, which resolves the default at session\n  build (adoptHealedDefault) and adopts the heal-reminted provider. A\n  session built before the heal keeps failing until a fresh one — the\n  narrowed, ADR-documented residual.\n- F2: the lost-update race between refreshStaleModels and the one-shot\n  background refresh is closed structurally: per-provider mergeSwap\n  (present-but-empty still removes — honest-empty preserved) + publishMu\n  serializing every post-Build snapshot publish.\n- F3 (CWE-918): redirect refusal now covers the INFERENCE path too —\n  openai.WithHTTPClient option + exported openaicompat.RefuseRedirects,\n  wired via newOpenAICompatEntry's variadic extra so it rides every\n  re-mint; gateway entry only. Anti-vacuous redirect test (bare-adapter\n  control leg must hit the attacker).\n- F4: healDefaultModel now re-mints caps/effort via the extracted\n  remintEntry (the third re-mint site) with entriesMu guarding the\n  entries map against request-path Lookup/Available races.\n- F5: stale provider-status remediation lines no longer render beneath an\n  unrelated ListModels error (state clear + render gate), and the error\n  state gained a next-action hint.\n- F6: sole-unreachable/unauthorized toolhive now promotes its real cause\n  into the /models empty state (beating both the generic and the\n  set-a-key notes) via promotedStatus + single-sourced providerStatusLine.\n- F7: \"(auto-selected)\" is now wire-driven (ProviderStatus.\n  default_model_auto_selected) instead of keyed on the provider name —\n  honest for operator-configured --default-model.\n- F8: toolhivellm's syscall.Stat_t split into detect_unix.go/\n  detect_other.go (fail-closed non-unix stub); GOOS=windows builds.\n- Cleanups: stripControl also strips Bidi_Control + U+2028/2029 (with\n  tests); remediation hints scoped to the toolhive provider so an\n  openrouter outage never records a thv-vendor hint; comment drift fixes;\n  Default() build-immutability trip-wire comment; client field renamed\n  DefaultModelAutoSelected.\n- ADR 0064: R2 addendums (heal reach, inference redirect coverage, the\n  provenance bit) + the favored direct-mode direction per review: a\n  thv llm token credential-helper + explicit endpoint config.\n\nNo new ADR-0027 inventory rows: publishMu/entriesMu are mutexes on the\nalready-inventoried registry; the auto-selected bit is derived state\nre-established by Build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KboCzrvXKCLEpfhgzB7SGf\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
