          "id": "610cc4befa985a269cefd75de512563a194bc9c0",
          "message": "fix(adapters): never put empty text content on the wire (#291)\n\nAn MCP fetch past the end of a document returned a tool result whose\nonly content was an empty text block. The stateless full-replay\nadapters re-serialized it every turn as an input_text with text:\"\",\nand the provider (Moonshot via OpenRouter, POST /responses) rejected\nevery request with 400 \"Invalid request: text content is empty\" —\npermanently bricking the session. The Anthropic Messages API rejects\nempty text blocks the same way.\n\nFix at request-build time (recorded history untouched, so already-\npoisoned persisted sessions heal on their next replay):\n\n- port.RouteToolResultParts drops text-summarised blocks whose\n  ToolBlockText render is empty (exact-empty rule, pinned in the doc\n  comment along with the caller contract for the nil→Content\n  fallback).\n- Both adapters substitute a deterministic \"(tool returned no\n  output)\" placeholder when the single-string tool-result fallback\n  would send empty content.\n- The anthropic adapter's four latent empty-text-block emitters\n  (malformed-image marker, degenerate empty user/assistant turns,\n  the RoleSystem fold) now emit honest non-empty placeholders.\n\nRegression tests reproduce the exact poison shape from the bricked\nsession and scan the marshaled request for \"text\":\"\". Non-empty\nserialization is byte-identical (prompt-cache prefix unchanged); no\nengine API surface change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
