          "message": "fix(models): close two carryover gaps found in post-merge review of #295 (#308)\n\nOpenRouter rides the same openai-adapter ItemID-dedup path as OpenAI, so\na cross-provider switch onto it hit the same \"Duplicate item\" collision\nthe OpenAI-specific synthesis was meant to prevent — gate on openrouter\ntoo, not just the literal \"openai\" provider id.\n\nA failed carryover create's enter-to-retry re-fires a plain, non-carryover\ncreate, but the switch-note armed by the original pick survived the\nfailure and falsely reported \"conversation kept\" on the retry's success.\nClear it in the restartFailedMsg reducer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
