          "message": "fix(openaichat): survive SSE keepalive frames (#309)\n\n* fix(openaichat): survive SSE keepalive frames\n\nA single SSE keepalive killed a streaming turn outright with\n\"agent: stream: unexpected end of JSON input\".\n\nThe openai-go ssestream decoder dispatches an Event on EVERY blank line\nand then json.Unmarshals the frame's accumulated data with no\nempty-payload check (packages/ssestream/ssestream.go:216). A frame\ncarrying no data therefore yields an EMPTY payload, and\njson.Unmarshal([]byte{}, ...) fails with \"unexpected end of JSON input\".\nStream.Next() latches that error and returns false forever, so one\nkeepalive ends the stream. Once text has already streamed the turn is\npost-commit, so the no-replay rule makes it TERMINAL rather than\nretried.\n\nOpenCode Go does exactly this on long turns, captured on the wire as:\n\n    : ping - 2026-07-26 19:11:49.346444+00:00\n\narriving at frame 496 of a streaming response. Of 20 captured streams\nexactly one contained a ping, and it is the only one that died — rare\nper request, fatal whenever it lands, which reads to an operator as\nfrequent unexplained failures.\n\nFix: a streaming line filter installed as the outermost middleware in\nNew(). It removes ONLY the blank line that would dispatch an empty\npayload, plus data: lines with an empty value (which would otherwise\nleave a stray \"\\n\" in the SDK's accumulator). Everything else passes\nthrough byte for byte, and it never buffers beyond the current line, so\nSSE arrival timing is preserved.\n\nMiddleware rather than ssestream.RegisterDecoder: that registry is a\npackage-level map written without a mutex, and this adapter is re-minted\nper session, so registering from a constructor would be a concurrent map\nwrite. Middleware is also content-type agnostic — the registry lookup\nuses the RAW header and silently misses \"text/event-stream; charset=utf-8\".\n\nScope is the opencode provider slot only (the sole openaichat.New\ncaller); openai/openrouter and anthropic use different adapters. Non-SSE\nbodies, including this gateway's text/plain error bodies, are untouched.\n\nTests use the captured bytes as a fixture and include an ORACLE (the\nunfiltered stream must still fail with the exact error, so this fails if\nupstream adds its own guard) and a WIRING test through the real\nconstructor -> middleware -> SDK path, mutation-verified: deleting the\noption.WithMiddleware line reproduces the production error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(openaichat): bound the SSE filter's per-line buffer\n\nThe filter added in the previous commit must see a line's terminator\nbefore it can decide whether the line survives, so it holds one line in\nmemory. Because it sits IN FRONT of ssestream's scanner, that scanner's\nown cap no longer engages first — so the filter as written REMOVED an\nexisting bound.\n\nMeasured against a newline-less stream:\n\n  ssestream's scanner (before the filter): errors at 32 MB with\n    \"bufio.Scanner: token too long\"\n  the filter (after):                      1126 MB buffered, 3338 MB\n    heap, in 5 seconds, and Read NEVER RETURNS\n\nllmresilience's idle watchdog would abort the read after\nStreamIdleTimeout, but at the observed throughput that is tens of GB —\nan OOM lands first.\n\nCap a single line at bufio.MaxScanTokenSize<<9 (32 MB), mirroring the\nSDK's scanner so the guard fails exactly where it would have rather than\nshifting the limit. Same posture as maxToolArgsBytes.\n\nerrSSELineTooLong is deliberately a PLAIN error — NOT a *json.SyntaxError\nand NOT wrapping io.ErrUnexpectedEOF — so llmresilience's\nDefaultClassifier treats it as non-retryable: a 32 MB line is a broken or\nhostile endpoint, not a transient truncation worth replaying. Pinned by a\ntest.\n\nThe oversized partial line is discarded before the error is latched, so\nRead's trailing-line flush (which exists so a genuinely truncated stream\nstill looks truncated) cannot emit it and thereby swallow the error.\n\nAn unexported maxLine field keeps the cap testable at 64 bytes instead of\n32 MB, without a mutable package-level global. Mutation-verified:\nremoving the bounds check fails TestKeepaliveFilterBoundsLineLength.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
