          "id": "587acabb6124308384a9763ce3e51ee70b01212f",
          "message": "feat(release): build and publish the mecatui image for brood-box (#302) (#317)\n\n* feat(release): ko-build the mecatui image with a brood-box agent manifest (#302)\n\nWire the dangling baseImageOverrides entry into a real build: a mecatui\nentry in .ko.yaml builds: (mirroring mecated/mecak8s, plus -X main.version\nfrom the VERSION env via ko's {{.Env.VERSION}} template) and\nko:build:mecatui / ko:publish:mecatui Taskfile tasks.\n\nThe image ships a self-describing brood-box manifest at\n/var/run/ko/agent.yaml via ko's per-package kodata mechanism, located by\nthe org.stacklok.broodbox.agent OCI config label (set with --image-label\nat build time). The manifest forwards all four provider keys and allows\negress to all four provider endpoints, matching internal/cliconfig's\nknownAuthProviders.\n\nThe brood-box wolfi base is now pinned by digest, matching the\ndefaultBaseImage reproducibility discipline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* ci(release): publish the mecatui image on every tag (#302)\n\nAdd a publish-mecatui job mirroring the publish job (same SHA-pinned\nactions, permissions, and sign/SBOM/SLSA-provenance scaffold), differing\nonly in the GHCR subpath (ghcr.io/.../mecatui), the ./cmd/mecatui build\ntarget, the mecatui OCI title, and the org.stacklok.broodbox.agent\n--image-label pointing at the embedded manifest. Multi-arch\n(linux/amd64,linux/arm64), tagged <version> + latest, keyless-signed.\n\nThe job is a separate parallel job rather than a reusable-workflow\nextraction: two instances with genuine non-parametric differences do not\nmeet the Rule of Three. The reusable-workflow pin check stays in publish\n(release-global, runs once).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs(release): document the mecatui container image (#302)\n\nAdd user-docs/deployment/mecatui.md (import into brood-box, the embedded\nmanifest, local ko build), a Container image / brood-box section in\ndocs/tui.md, and flip the cut-release skill + workflows README + the\nrelease.yml header to the two-image release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
