          "id": "49678914582be01c3c163e64c99259812df1c2f1",
          "message": "refactor(discovery): graduate agent-def + skills discovery into engine/adapter (#328) (#333)\n\n* refactor(discovery): graduate agent-def + skills discovery into engine/adapter (#328)\n\nMove the two filesystem discovery adapters into the importable engine\nmodule, following the fstools (#269) graduation pattern:\n\n- engine/adapter/agentfs — the whole of internal/adapter/agents\n  (.claude/agents discovery, frontmatter parser, FSSource, MultiSource,\n  registry). engine/adapter/skillfs — the READ-ONLY skills core\n  (.claude/skills discovery, FSSource, the Skill tool body, activator,\n  injection scanner). The writable SkillDraft half stays in root and\n  reaches the core through the alias.\n- Carried helpers live in per-package carry.go files, pinned\n  byte-identical to their internal/adapter/{toolkit,xdgconfig,osfs}\n  origins (the engine module must not import the root module).\n- The one osfs edge (read-root canonicalisation) is broken by carrying\n  osfs.resolveRoot verbatim into skillfs — no osfs import.\n- skillfs.NewSourceActivator now takes an unexported consumer-side\n  assetProvisioner interface; root *AssetMaterializer satisfies it\n  implicitly. skillfs exports ParseSkill for the root promotion gate.\n- Root internal/adapter/{agents,skills} become thin alias shims (the\n  internal/adapter/tools pattern); no second copy to drift.\n- engine/go.mod gains a direct require on go.yaml.in/yaml/v3 (both\n  frontmatter parsers use it; operator-approved). ADR 0036 + AGENTS.md\n  closure sentences updated (also picking up robfig/cron).\n- New depguard blocks allow os (discovery is filesystem-walking) and\n  deny os/exec. COMPATIBILITY.md lists both under the engine/adapter/*\n  exclusion; no CHANGELOG entry per the fstools precedent.\n- Panel review fix: the four hand-rolled UTF8RuneStart copies were\n  byte-identical to stdlib utf8.RuneStart — deleted in toolkit, fstools,\n  agentfs, skillfs.\n\nVerified: task lint, task test (incl. GOWORK=off engine-standalone),\ntask api:check, cmd/mecademo, task site:build, plus a throwaway\nGOWORK=off consumer module in .scratch resolving both .claude/agents\nand .claude/skills fixtures through the new packages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* test(e2e): live coverage for Subagent(agent=…) via a workspace agent def (#328)\n\nThe live suite exercised skill activation and generic subagents but never\na NAMED agent definition — the agentfs half of the graduation. Add a\nfixture def (e2e/fixtures/agents/fruit-reader.md, scoped tools: Read)\nlaid out at <workspace>/.claude/agents/ by the harness, and a spec that\ndelegates Subagent(agent=\"fruit-reader\") and asserts on EVENTS: the call\nnames the def, the result succeeds with the agentId trailer and carries\nthe FRUIT.txt fact, the child ends stop=end_turn, and no approval\nsurfaces. The child's own Read is deliberately not asserted — child tool\ncalls stay on the child stream (gauntlet #7).\n\nVerified live against OpenRouter (focused run, incl. the two pre-existing\nskills specs as a fixture-change smoke check).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>",
