          "message": "feat(prompt): RulesSource port + .claude/rules discovery (#329) (#334)\n\n* feat(prompt): RulesSource port + .claude/rules discovery — path-scoped rules reach turn-0 context (#329)\n\n.claude/rules/*.md was discovered by nothing in mecatl: a repo that\nfollowed Claude Code's own guidance (split CLAUDE.md past ~200 lines\ninto .claude/rules/) silently lost every rule it split out. This closes\nthe last unimplemented .claude/* convention through a public port, per\nADR 0081:\n\n- engine/prompt: the RulesSource port + Rule value object + RuleOrigin\n  (consumer-local, the SoulSource/CommandSource precedent) and the\n  RulesAssembler on the InstructionAssembler seam — eager v1: all rules\n  injected at turn 0 as ONE user-role message, each fenced with its\n  paths: globs stated as a model-applied \"Applies when:\" condition.\n  20 KiB/rule + 40 KiB combined + 32-count caps, fail-soft, never aborts\n  a run. IsInjectedTurn0Fragment recognises the fragment.\n- engine/adapter/rulesfs: the FS implementation (flat <name>.md, the\n  agentfs structural twin) — project tiers (.mecatl/rules, .claude/rules)\n  trust-gated on IncludeProjectTier, user tiers (XDG + ~/.claude/rules)\n  always active. paths: parses as a YAML sequence with scalar/comma\n  tolerance. sourceconformance gains the RunRulesSource suite + fixture.\n- Composition: resolveRulesSeam resolves ONCE at Build and threads the\n  same assembler into shared + per-session engines (the issue-#42 drift\n  class), with the trust-gate WITHHELD WARN and the ENABLED/DISABLED\n  build-once facts.\n- NO FLAGS (operator decision, ADR 0081 §5): conventional discovery is\n  always-on like AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md themselves — the conventional lanes\n  are inert without dirs and TrustProject is the one gate.\n- Live e2e: a rules fixture + spec asserting the deterministic\n  \"rules ENABLED\" build fact (plus a quarantined behavioural marker),\n  verified live against OpenRouter.\n\nPanel review (Spec/Standards/Security/Architecture/reuse/duplication +\nQA): zero ship-blockers. Applied findings: stale origin-extraction\ntrip-wire comment updated in agentsource.go (the third seam arrived and\nextraction was deferred — the label sets differ); rule names sanitized\nbefore fence interpolation (CWE-74 hardening); fence-structure test\nassertions strengthened; skillfs gained the missing carry-parity pin.\nDeferred: factory-path variant of TestPerSessionAssemblerMatchesShared\n(the capture is structural; the behavioural test proves no doubling).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate llms.txt after ADR 0081 review edits\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* test(e2e): cover the untrusted-workspace rules path (#329)\n\nThe live suite only exercised the trusted lane (the harness always\nspawns with --trust-project), leaving the trust gate — the ONE boundary\nfor always-on rules discovery (ADR 0081 §5) — proven only offline. Add\na spec spawning a second mecated with --trust-project=false (flag pkg\nlast-wins) asserting the project-tier-withheld WARN and the ABSENCE of\n\"rules ENABLED\" — a regression here means a malicious repo's\n.claude/rules reaches the model. Also correct the spawn comment: the\nflag is load-bearing for agent defs and rules, not just \"skills + any\nproject allows\".\n\nVerified live against OpenRouter (focused runs of all three rules\nspecs).\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>",
