          "id": "ef590dcfb39fb2ca525b58704095f34ad96a7abf",
          "message": "feat(cli): simplify mecated and mecatui configuration (#355)\n\n* feat(cli): add explicit mecated commands\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(cli): add progressive mecated help\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* refactor(prompt): remove output economy control\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(tui): add explicit local and connect modes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(config): add explicit daemon config\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(config): add daemon config tooling\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* test(config): cover daemon config compatibility\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(mecatui): bare = deterministic embedded, connect-only subcommand\n\nClean break per ADR 0085: bare mecatui hosts the embedded server and\nnever probes loopback; mecatui connect ADDRESS is the only subcommand.\nDelete the local subcommand, the --server flag, the probe transport\npath, and every legacy warning/alias. Usage errors now print the\ntop-level command summary; client/probe.go is orphaned and removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(mecated): require serve/acp, bare invocation is a usage error\n\nClean break per ADR 0085: bare mecated prints help and exits non-zero\n(two mutually-exclusive transports, no canonical alias); --acp is\ndeleted outright. Leading -h/--help/--help-all prints top-level help\nand exits 0. deploy/ and the e2e harness spawn mecated serve.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* feat(cli)!: delete output-economy shims; ADR 0085 clean-break grammar\n\n--output-economy is an unknown flag in all three mains; output-economy:\nin settings.yaml is a targeted unknown-key error naming the key. No\nmigration window, no warning-only parse. ADR 0085 records the clean\nbreak, superseding ADR 0083's staged transport migration and ADR 0082\ndecision item 4. All docs/user-docs/README lead with the canonical\nforms; llms.txt regenerated. Orphaned cliconfig.PrintDefaultsHide\nremoved.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: legacy spellings are rejected: bare mecated,\nmecated --acp, mecatui local, mecatui --server, --output-economy,\noutput-economy:.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs: renumber PR ADRs to 0086-0089, fix review findings\n\nThe PR's new ADRs collided with 0082-factory-mcp-wiring on main;\nrenumber 0082/0083/0084/0085 -> 0086/0087/0088/0089 and rewire every\npointer (supersession headers, index, living docs, code comments).\n\nDocs-review fixes: stale bare-mecated invocations in model-routing /\nworkspace-trust / http-sse-api / README; --yolo is rejected (not\nignored) in connect mode; README cites mecated acp, not the deleted\n--acp flag; drop the deleted IsReachable mention; document the\nbare-mecated help+exit-2 contract and the connect --help carve-out;\ndaemon-config ADR drops the legacy-spelling parenthetical and the\nnon-existent SHA citations; user-docs ADR link uses the github blob\nURL (ADRs are not site-published); remove the output-economy migration\nsection (clean break, no assist prose); copy nits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* docs: retitle renumbered ADRs 0086-0089 in-page\n\nThe renumber commit renamed the files but not the in-page headings and\nrelative links, breaking the matlatl gate in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>",
