          "id": "b5b328d43ad3711a0fa46ef941d7149f94f8f3f5",
          "message": "feat(cliconfig): per-server --mcp-server-insecure-http opt-in, order-independent (#360)\n\n* feat(cliconfig): per-server --mcp-server-insecure-http opt-in, order-independent (#358)\n\nMCPServerList.Set no longer runs the token-bearing scheme gate inline:\nentries are collected during parse and the CWE-319 gate runs in a new\npost-parse Finalize step the three mains (mecated, mecatequi, mecak8s)\ncall right after flag.Parse — so the new repeatable\n--mcp-server-insecure-http <name> relaxation composes with --mcp-server\nregardless of argv order (the titlani#40 contract addition).\n\nThe relaxation applies ONLY to the named server (same ^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$\nname grammar as #347), ONLY to the http scheme; an unknown name, or a\nname whose URL is https/loopback/non-http, is a loud error (a stale\nacknowledgment is never silently inert). Default posture unchanged: a\ntoken-bearing http non-loopback URL without the relaxation still fails.\nServers() panics fail-closed before a successful Finalize.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: ADR 0090 + operator docs for --mcp-server-insecure-http (#358)\n\nNew ADR 0090 records the per-server plain-http opt-in decision, the\nrejected proxy-sidecar alternative (satisfies the gate without changing\nwire security), the rejected global escape hatch, and the\norder-independence requirement from titlani#40. Factory invocation\nprofile (docs/usage/mecatequi-ci.md), the mecated/mecak8s flag tables,\nand the user-docs MCP pages state the acknowledgment plainly: cleartext\non the network path; network-layer controls + short-lived tokens are\nthe operator's mitigations. llms.txt regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
