          "id": "f67fcb1552241513a36004a30a12480e10fe40f9",
          "message": "feat(search): graduate WebSearch tool + providers into engine/adapter (#363)\n\nThe engine module shipped the web-search PORT (tool.SearchProvider and its\nsentinels) but no tool body and no concrete provider — both lived in the root\nmodule's internal/, unimportable. Engine consumers had to reimplement the\ncorrectness- and security-critical logic (LLM01 fencing, the\nErrSearchUnavailable-vs-ErrSearchBackendDown degradation, result clamping) and\nre-derive the per-backend HTTP glue (Exa / generic HTTP / SearXNG / Brave).\n\nGraduate both halves into engine/adapter/search/, following the #269 fstools\nprecedent:\n\n- websearch.go (tool body) — imports engine/agent for agent.FenceUntrusted\n  (the single-source-of-truth untrusted-content fence) and carries the small\n  toolkit helpers locally (fstools carry pattern), so the engine module never\n  imports the root module.\n- exasearch.go + httpsearch.go (providers) — verbatim; stdlib +\n  x/sync/semaphore + engine/tool only, so engine/go.mod's require block does\n  not grow.\n- internal/adapter/tools keeps a thin WebSearchTool/NewWebSearchTool alias so\n  existing callers compile unchanged; internal/adapter/search/ is deleted and\n  internal/app now imports engine/adapter/search directly.\n\nThe depguard engine-adapter-search rule is widened (engine/agent +\nengine/session + x/sync/semaphore) with a NOTE recording the accepted dep-cone\ncost of importing the agent loop for the fence, and a follow-up to relocate the\nfence primitives to engine/governance. Docs citations, engine/CHANGELOG, and\nengine/COMPATIBILITY updated; a framing-header whole-line-prevention assertion\nadded to the adversarial injection test.",
