          "id": "209b07fad3d2d55a1609a858ff61b6ca77dba4c7",
          "message": "feat(schedule): in-flight fire state, progress, and wall-clock timeout (#386) (#400)\n\n* feat(schedule): in-flight fire state model + StopTimeout + store adapters (#386)\n\nPhase 1+2 of the in-flight scheduled-fire lifecycle. Today a claimed fire\nis invisible until RecordFire: inspect renders \"fires: none\" while one\nruns (ambiguous: running / stuck / crashed / RecordFire-failed), and the\nminted sched-- session id is only discoverable after the run completes.\n\nPromote the in-flight fire to a first-class persisted stage:\n\n- engine/port/schedule.go: ScheduleState gains LastFireStartedAt /\n  LastFireProgressAt / FireDeadline; ScheduleFire gains StartedAt /\n  ProgressAt / Deadline; ScheduleSpec gains FireTimeout (per-fire\n  wall-clock deadline knob). ScheduleStore gains RecordFireStart (persist\n  the in-flight fire + stamp the real session id early) and\n  RecordFireProgress (advance the last-progress timestamp). RecordFire\n  flips terminal + clears the in-flight fields; Claim/ClaimNow zero them.\n- engine/session: new StopTimeout StopReason (\"timeout\") — a clean,\n  recoverable wall-clock-deadline terminal (StopBudget sibling), string\n  passthrough on the wire.\n- memschedulestore (reference) + jsonlstore + redisstore implement the\n  two methods; the scheduleconformance suite gains 5 in-flight subtests\n  (persist-start, idempotent, progress-advances, record-clears,\n  claim-alone-leaves-zero) and all three backends pass.\n- engine/api/*.txt regenerated; engine/CHANGELOG.md notes the Added\n  (minor) surface.\n\nComposition wiring (fire lifecycle, wall-clock enforcement, started\nnotice, stale reconcile) lands in the next commit.\n\n* feat(schedule): fire lifecycle — early start persist, wall-clock deadline, progress (#386)\n\nPhase 3 wires the in-flight lifecycle into the composition FireFunc\n(makeFireFunc):\n\n- Early persistence: after CreateSessionWithProfile, RecordFireStart\n  stamps the real sched-- session id + StartedAt + the computed Deadline\n  (best-effort WARN on failure; the at-most-once Claim already advanced).\n- Wall-clock deadline: a time.AfterFunc watchdog cancels the in-flight\n  run via the blessed Service.Cancel/run.Cancel seam after\n  effectiveFireDeadline (spec.FireTimeout, else defaultFireTimeout=30m).\n  A deadline-fired run that drained to StopCancelled is overridden to\n  StopTimeout with an Err naming the timeout; the session settles to a\n  recoverable terminal snapshot via settleFireTerminalSnapshot.\n- Progress: RecordFireProgress fires on EvToolCall/EvTurnEnd/EvResult\n  (not per chunk), advancing LastFireProgressAt.\n- Create-failure after Claim still records a terminal StopError fire.\n\nstartScheduler rediscovers the ScheduleStore and threads it + the default\ntimeout into makeFireFunc (storage-agnostic). Tests cover early-persist,\nStopTimeout on deadline, progress advance, and create-failure terminal.\n\n* feat(schedule): deliver a harness-authored fire-started notice (#386)\n\nPhase 4a. The originating conversation now gets a lightweight, fenced-\nuntrusted, harness-authored notice when a fire STARTS (schedule name +\nfire id + session id), distinct from the terminal result report — the\noperator sees \"it triggered, here's the fire\" instead of silence until\ncompletion.\n\ndeliverFireStarted mirrors deliverFireResult: enqueues to the same\nDeliveryQueue exactly-once ledger with a distinct \"started\" header so it\nnever duplicates or collides with the terminal note, state-aware\n(busy/awaiting origin enqueues only, empty origin no-op), and carries NO\nmodel-authored fire content. makeFireFunc invokes it (nil-safe) right\nafter the early RecordFireStart; wired in startScheduler. Tests cover\nenqueue-with-ids, busy/awaiting enqueue-only, empty-origin no-op,\nnon-duplication of the terminal note, and fenced harness-authored body.\n\n* feat(schedule): reconcile stale fires after a process crash (#386)\n\nPhase 4b. A crashed process's claimed-but-never-terminal fire is now\ndistinguishable from a live run after restart, instead of sitting\n\"pending\"/in-flight forever.\n\nThe scheduler detects stale in-flight state store-only (pending sentinel\npast the window, or a real in-flight fire whose prior-fire lease is no\nlonger live and whose start is past the window); a genuinely-live fire\n(lease held) is never reconciled. Reconciliation is a composition-injected\nReconcileStaleFire callback (the scheduler stays storage-agnostic, never\nimporting the server) that settles the two crash cases: crash-after-Claim\nrecords a terminal StopError fire; crash-after-session settles the session\nto cancelled (Interrupt-recoverable) and records StopError.\n\nAlso fix TestFireDelivery_EmbeddedEndToEnd: it now waits for the terminal\n\"completed with stop reason:\" marker specifically, since the new started\nnotice shares the \"[scheduled task \" prefix and would otherwise satisfy\nthe looser match first.\n\n* feat(schedule): surface in-flight fire state on inspect, wire, and TUI (#386)\n\nPhase 5 makes the in-flight fire VISIBLE and keeps the three surfaces\n(agent inspect / gRPC+HTTP / TUI overlay) in agreement.\n\n- renderScheduleInspect (engine/agent): a claimed fire (pending sentinel,\n  run not started) renders \"in-flight: claimed (session pending)\" instead\n  of the ambiguous \"fires: none\"; an in-flight fire (Stop empty) renders\n  the in-flight marker + started/last-progress/deadline; a schedule-level\n  in-flight summary shows when a live fire exists. fire_timeout surfaces\n  in the spec summary.\n- schedule.proto: ScheduleState + last_fire_started_at /\n  last_fire_progress_at / fire_deadline; ScheduleFire + started_at /\n  progress_at / deadline; ScheduleSpec + fire_timeout (Duration).\n  Regenerated contracts/gen.\n- grpc_schedule.go: all four wire mappers project the new fields (the ONE\n  projection path gRPC + HTTP share).\n- TUI overlay: client structs + mappers carry the fields; the inspect\n  render mirrors the agent (in-flight marker, claimed-pending, never\n  \"no fires recorded\" when claimed).\n\nTests: agent render (in-flight / claimed-pending / never-fired /\nterminal), a wire-projection test driving the real store, and TUI render.\n\n* docs(schedule): ADR 0097 + notes for in-flight fire state (#386)\n\n- docs/adr/0097-scheduled-fire-inflight-state.md (new): the in-flight\n  fire as a first-class persisted lifecycle stage; early session-id\n  persistence; progress timestamps; the wall-clock deadline + StopTimeout;\n  the started notice; the storage-agnostic detect-in-scheduler /\n  reconcile-in-composition stale-fire seam.\n- docs/adr/README.md: index row.\n- docs/design/IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md: \"In-flight fire state\" paragraph.\n- docs/adr/0027-cloud-native.md: List-1 re-audit (no new row; the state\n  lives in the durable store).\n- docs/usage/mecated.md: the fire_timeout spec field + in-flight inspect.\n- user-docs/what-you-get/scheduled-tasks.md: \"Watching a fire while it\n  runs\" (in-flight state, timeout, started notice, crash recovery).\n- llms.txt regenerated.\n\n* fix(schedule): atomic targeted fire-progress writes (#386 review)\n\nTwo Medium findings from the #386 panel:\n\n- RecordFireProgress now takes the fire ID (RecordFireProgress(ctx, name,\n  fireID, at)) so the caller passes the known id instead of the store\n  scanning for the in-flight fire. jsonlstore writes the single fire file\n  directly (no ReadDir scan under the store mutex on every turn boundary);\n  redisstore addresses the single key (no SCAN); memschedulestore looks it\n  up directly. Engine-port widening; engine/CHANGELOG.md amended.\n- redisstore's progress write is now an atomic Lua CAS (byte-compare\n  optimistic lock) so a concurrent terminal RecordFire landing mid-write\n  can never revert a terminal record back to in-flight (the cross-replica\n  lease-lapse race). The \"Stop empty\" guard + the byte-compare together\n  guarantee the terminal record wins.\n\nConformance gains two subtests across all three backends: progress targets\nthe named fire only, and progress never reverts a terminal fire.",
