          "message": "fix(build): bump Go toolchain to 1.26.6 (govulncheck gate) (#516)\n\nThe CI govulncheck gate started failing across the board (not tied to\nany particular PR) once GO-2026-5026, GO-2026-5972, GO-2026-6088,\nGO-2026-6089, GO-2026-6090, GO-2026-6091, and GO-2026-6218 landed in\nthe vuln DB — all seven are Go 1.26.5 stdlib CVEs (net/http, crypto/tls,\nencoding/asn1, encoding/xml, html/template, net, net/url), fixed in\n1.26.6. Bump the `go` directive in every module (root, engine, authn/oidc,\neach provider/*) and go.work so CI's go-version-file resolution picks up\nthe patched toolchain. Verified locally: govulncheck no longer reports\nany of the seven ids as reachable findings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
