          "id": "d2b324fae8c86b3c84965d0ce96bcfaa7a9e7744",
          "message": "feat(subagent): project live usage and monotonic tool counts on running children (#569)\n\nA running subagent's fleet roster row and inline card showed ↑0 ↓0 tokens\nand a tool count that reset to zero mid-run, until the child terminated.\n\nROOT CAUSE — two self-inflicted protocol gaps in drainChildObserved (the\nsingle filter/redact chokepoint between a child's private event stream and\nthe parent's observability projection):\n\n1. It dropped the child's EvTurnEnd events, the only mid-run carrier of\n   token usage (TurnEndPayload.Usage). Only the terminal EvResult.Usage\n   crossed, onto subagent.end — hence zero until the end.\n2. It stamped SubagentPayload.ToolCount on only SOME projection kinds\n   (tool.result / result), leaving tool.call, message.delta, and the new\n   turn.end projections carrying an unset 0. Consumers assigned the field\n   unconditionally, so each non-count projection reset the displayed count\n   to zero. The field's doc (\"the running or final number of tool calls\")\n   gave no signal its validity was InnerKind-conditional — that misreading\n   was the bug.\n\nTHE FIX — make the two totals unconditional rather than conditional:\n\n- Project the child's EvTurnEnd through the same subagent.tool channel so\n  usage surfaces mid-run.\n- Stamp ToolCount and Usage as CUMULATIVE running totals on EVERY projection\n  (the engine knows both at every emit point). The fields are now truthful\n  on every event; consumers assign freely with no InnerKind guard and no\n  reset is possible.\n- ToolCount now counts tools STARTED (incremented at tool.call, not\n  tool.result — a result may never arrive on a cancel, and the old\n  result-time increment was exactly why intermediate projections carried a\n  stale 0). Semantic note: the roster/card \"N tools\" now reads\n  \"N started\", including an in-flight tool.\n- Usage stays provider-truth-only: the issue-#82 display-only estimate is\n  never folded into the cumulative figure.\n- Both field docs collapse to a one-line cumulative contract; the TUI\n  consumers (fleetTool, addSubagentTool, SubagentMsg doc) drop their guards.\n- Gauntlet #7 holds: ToolCount/Usage are harness/provider metadata, never\n  child-authored content; nothing enters the parent Conversation. No proto\n  change — the projected Usage rides the existing Subagent.Usage field.\n\nTESTS: TestSubagentProjectsLiveUsage (two-turn child projects 10/4 then 16/6\nmid-run, terminal agrees) and TestSubagentLiveUsageDoesNotResetToolCount\n(totals current on every projection, count monotonic through interleaving).\nThe four subagent overlay goldens asserted the old reset shape; refreshed to\nthe monotonic behavior. Full engine/session/mecatui suites + vet green.\n\nRefs #568 (the opt-in raw child-transcript tool, a separate security-gated\nfollow-up; this stays in the bounded observability tier).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
