          "id": "bb1bcd1c411d7e021aed1e83305a548e33f74a94",
          "message": "fix(mecatui): load operator mcp.servers in embedded mode (#658) (#660)\n\nmecatui's embedded server wired no MCPProfileLoader, so the operator-tier\nmcp.servers block from ~/.config/mecatl/settings.yaml was parsed by\npermconfig and silently discarded before app.Build ever saw it. The three\nheadless binaries (mecated, mecatequi, mecak8s) were wired when the\nloader was added in #562; mecatui was missed.\n\nWire NewMCPProfileResolver(nil, os.LookupEnv) so operator settings activate\nunder the TUI's embedded server with no flag required — the legacy\n--mcp-server flag stays off per the original heavier-opt-in intent.\n\nAlso add a composition-level WARN: any consumer omitting the loader gets a\nsettings-only diagnostic (count only, never server names/URLs/tokens), so\nthe silent-drop is now loud for future consumers.\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@mecatl.dev>",
