          "id": "b27d4bfe17b13ba20538b70eb78540228bb257b8",
          "message": "feat(release): publish deploy/helm/mecak8s chart to GHCR (#768)\n\n* feat(release): publish deploy/helm/mecak8s chart to GHCR\n\nAdd a publish-helm-chart job to release.yml that packages the\nmecak8s Helm chart, versions it from the release tag (no Chart.yaml\nbump needed), pushes it to oci://ghcr.io/stacklok/mecatl/charts, and\ncosign-signs the digest — mirroring stacklok/atrium's helm-publish.yml\nso stacklok/infra's Flux GitOps pipeline has a published OCI artifact\nto point a HelmRepository at (#767).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(release): clarify id-token permission is cosign-only\n\nThe comment attributed id-token: write to both \"ghcr login\" and cosign\nsigning, but ghcr login (helm registry login + docker/login-action)\nauthenticates with the packages-write-backed GITHUB_TOKEN, not OIDC.\nid-token: write is consumed only by cosign sign's Fulcio exchange.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate llms.txt after README.md changes\n\ntask docs:llms was missed when documenting the new publish-helm-chart\njob in .github/workflows/README.md — the CI Docs (matlatl) job caught\nthe stale heading count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
