          "id": "7452ae9e1534fe70aa37fd0a34f6614f78a43023",
          "message": "feat(mecak8s): add extraEnv passthrough for real LLM provider wiring (#782)\n\nWithout mockProvider or a real provider credential, the binary hard-\nfails at startup (internal/app/registry.go's errNoProvider — confirmed\nby tracing buildProviderRegistryContext), and the chart had no\nmechanism to supply one at all: no env passthrough, no API-key secret\nmount, no --default-provider flag. extraEnv (a raw EnvVar list,\nmatching atrium's chart) closes that gap generically: project any\nSecret's key as e.g. OPENROUTER_API_KEY via valueFrom.secretKeyRef.\ncliconfig detects the env var directly and, with a single key present,\nselects that provider as the default automatically (no\n--default-provider needed) — confirmed via\ninternal/app/registry.go's preferredDefaultProvider.\n\nThe same values shape works identically in any deployment (Kind, a\nreal cluster, ...) — only the referenced Secret's provenance differs\n(kubectl create secret vs. an ExternalSecret).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-27T12:30:01+02:00",
