          "id": "9062857316a6787ba1090af15e0cb96ec9bdb52a",
          "message": "feat(mecak8s-vmcp): wire a real provider into the Kind fixture via extraEnv (#787)\n\nchart-apply now checks OPENROUTER_API_KEY (same convention task e2e:k8s\nalready documents): when set, it upserts a Secret and re-installs the\nchart with --set extraEnv[...] pointing at it, so a single API key\nflips the fixture from the mock provider to a real one. When unset,\nbehavior is byte-identical to before.\n\nAlso drops chart-apply's internal:true so it can be re-run standalone\nagainst an already-running cluster (e.g. to flip a live key) without\nredoing kind-setup's whole pipeline (namespace, cert-manager, image\nbuild, Dex).\n\nVerified by extracting the rendered shell script (task --summary\nchart-apply) and running it against mocked kubectl/helm binaries: the\nmock-only path is unchanged, and the live path creates the Secret\nbefore helm runs and appends exactly the three expected --set flags,\nwith the API key never appearing on the helm command line.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
