          "id": "583b86052549de7b571a5f68628790d92d45cb65",
          "message": "feat(mecatui): scheduled tasks Phase 3a — /schedule slash command + overlay (#239)\n\n* feat(mecatui): scheduled tasks Phase 3a — /schedule slash command + overlay (#234)\n\nAdd the mecatui interactive schedule-management surface, a peer of the\nexisting /agents, /team, and /worktrees overlays. The server-side wire\n(Phase 2a ScheduleService gRPC + Phase 2b settings.yaml/CLI) already\nshipped; this lands the client + TUI overlay.\n\n- contracts/proto: ServerCapabilities.scheduling (bool, additive) gates the\n  overlay; independent of the --scheduler tick loop (the store-backed RPCs\n  work without auto-firing). Regenerated via task generate.\n- internal/adapter/server: capabilities() sets Scheduling from\n  scheduleStore() != nil (the RPCs are functional as long as a ScheduleStore\n  is reachable).\n- cmd/mecatui/client: new schedule.go — proto-free mirror of the schedule\n  wire surface (Schedule/ScheduleSpec/ScheduleState/ScheduleFire + Msg\n  types + ScheduleLister interface + 8 tea.Cmd constructors); Client gains a\n  scheduleSvc stub; Capabilities gains Scheduling. CreateSchedule/GetFire\n  exported for the planned Phase 3b in-overlay Create form (documented as\n  uncalled in v1).\n- cmd/mecatui/ui: new schedule.go — the overlay (scheduleView enum:\n  none/panel/confirm/inspect; scheduleState; open/close/onScheduleKey/\n  updateScheduleMsg/renderScheduleOverlay + helpers). Panel lists schedules\n  (name, trigger summary, enabled, next/last fire, fire count) with\n  type-to-filter + cursor nav. Action keys: enter=inspect (loads fires via\n  ListFires), p=pause, r=resume, f=fire-now, d=delete (confirm sub-view).\n  All server-derived fields sanitized via sanitizeTerminal at the render\n  boundary (triggerSummary included). /schedule builtin registered after\n  /worktrees, gated on caps.Scheduling && deps.Sched wired. updateInventoryMsgs\n  widened to (Model, Cmd, bool) so the action-success re-list cmd propagates.\n- Tests: client/schedule_test.go (mappers + RPC wrappers + Cmd constructors,\n  success + error arms); ui/schedule_test.go (open/nil-guard/filter/pause-\n  resume-fire-delete/inspect-loads-fires/confirm-delete-backout/error-render/\n  mid-run-guard/esc-close/trigger-summary); builtins_test.go caps-filter +\n  by-name cases; help goldens refreshed.\n- Docs: PRODUCTION-READINESS.md flips Phase 3a to shipped (NL→cron deferred\n  to v2); tui.md adds the /schedule section + palette entry; usage.md flips\n  the planned line to shipped. llms.txt regenerated.\n\nIn-scope scope note: the issue lists Create as a Phase 3a action; this lands\nlist/inspect/pause/resume/fire-now/delete and defers the in-overlay Create\nFORM to Phase 3b (raw cron/one-shot entry via the CLI/settings.yaml already\nworks; the composer form is the follow-up). FireNow and Delete are useful\npeer actions added beyond the literal pause/resume list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Osorio Ortiz <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(mecatui): /schedule — /-to-filter so action keys aren't stolen by the filter\n\nReview follow-ups on #239:\n\n- The /schedule panel focused its filter input on open while also binding bare-rune\n  action keys (p/r/f/d), so those letters could never be typed into the filter and\n  instead fired pause/resume/fire-now/delete — f/p/r with no confirmation. Switch to\n  a /-to-filter model: the panel opens in action mode; `/` focuses the filter, and\n  esc/enter exit filter mode keeping the narrowed value. Render the filter line so\n  the mode is visible, and update the footer + docs/tui.md. Add\n  TestScheduleFilterModeDoesNotFireActions, which drives keys through onScheduleKey\n  in both modes — the collision the old tests (SetValue-driven filter vs\n  router-driven actions) never exercised together.\n- Replace the hand-rolled itoa with strconv.Itoa (the \"avoids pulling in fmt\"\n  rationale was wrong: strconv.Itoa does not import fmt).\n- Rename misfireFromString -> misfireStringFromProto (it maps enum->string, not the\n  reverse; its sibling misfireToProtoFromString is already named for its direction).\n- Correct the stale scheduleState \"never mutated in place\" comment (the ScheduleMsg\n  Get-refresh updates a single element in place; filtered is always rebuilt).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jakub Hrozek <jakub@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
