          "id": "2d087fe837f8b753939d267ff053f419f9397948",
          "message": "fix(mcp): suppress top-level type-mismatch warning for array/primitive structuredContent (#244)\n\nWhen an MCP tool returns a JSON array or primitive as its structuredContent\nand advertised an object-only outputSchema, validateStructuredContent called\nresolved.Validate(instance), which returned a top-level type-mismatch error\nsurfaced to the model as a misleading [structured output validation warning]\nnote. The structured content itself still rode through as a block, but the\nwarning read like a failure.\n\nThe MCP spec's \"must marshal to a JSON object\" is a SHOULD, not a hard\ncontract; a valid JSON value of any shape is acceptable structuredContent.\nCallMcpWithQuery and the callTool/jqInputPreview/isStructuredResult paths\nwere already array-safe (they decode into any). Only the validation note\nwas wrong.\n\nvalidateStructuredContent now suppresses a top-level type mismatch (array/\nprimitive vs an object-only schema) via a new isTopLevelTypeMismatch\nclassifier + jsonInstanceType probe, mirroring the jsonschema-go validator's\nown early-return gate and number-subsumes-integer rule. Field-level\nviolations inside a matching shape still surface as warnings — those are a\ngenuine misbehaving-server signal.\n\nTests: direct table tests for the helpers (every branch: array/primitive/\nnull/boolean vs object, multi-type Types, integer/number subsumption,\njson.RawMessage, empty schema), the regression integration test\n(TestMapContentStructuredContentArrayAgainstObjectSchema), a primitive-\nagainst-object-schema integration test, CallMcpWithQuery array/primitive\njq tests, and a callTool array round-trip test.\n\nDocs: softened \"JSON object\" to \"JSON value (object, array, or primitive)\"\nand \"schema-validated view\" to \"typed view\" in ADRs 0059/0063 and\nIMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md (factual correction — the behavior was always\narray-accepting; the language was imprecise).",
