          "id": "eec03d99c6f682d63a00281449aa2e1fa47783d8",
          "message": "docs: cloud-native harness systems — future work scoping (#54)\n\n* docs: cloud-native harness kit subsystem inventory (speculative)\n\nScoping doc inventorying the subsystems mecatl would break out to become a\n\"cloud-native harness\" — externalized state, separable tool execution, a\nnear-stateless and cheaply restartable process. Tier A (six stateful/execution\nsubsystems, including resource-lifetime management as the one seam not yet\nbuilt) + Tier B (already-clean ports) + a priority synthesis. Headers are\nnumbered for reference.\n\nSpeculative / not a committed direction; unsure this repo is its home.\n\nRebased onto main (987d88d) and re-verified against it: records the base\ncommit it was first written against (a1baf7ee), corrects the internal/ → engine/\ncore move, and annotates where the shipped driver-seams arc (DRIVERS.md) has\nturned \"where to explore\" predictions into implemented reality — gRPC drivers\nfor SessionStore (+ PrunableStore retention), MemoryStore, and the\nskill/soul/agent/command sources, with the workspace/FS driver left as the one\nsketched-not-built seam. Also: failed-session recovery, the no-FS profile,\nchild-session GC, and Message.ProviderPhase in the snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: distill cloud-native kit inventory into a future-work scoping doc\n\nADR 0027 (cloud-native arc, shipped) and ADR 0048 (mecak8s, shipped) have since\nresolved most of what docs/design/CLOUD-NATIVE-KIT.md was scoping: durable event\nlog, mid-turn awaiting-approval resume, cross-process session leasing, and a\nconcrete k8s-native demonstration. Replace the 952-line speculative inventory\nwith docs/cloud-native-harness-systems.md, which keeps only what's still\ngenuinely unscoped (the filesystem/forker/command-runner shared-handle problem,\nforking-as-environment-descent, execution-as-a-service, and two small\ndomain-logic gaps) and points at the ADRs for everything else. Linked from\ndocs/cloud-native-harness-kit.md; llms.txt regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop references to the superseded doc in cloud-native-harness-systems.md\n\nGit already has the history (the deleted docs/design/CLOUD-NATIVE-KIT.md and\nPR #54); no need to narrate it inside the doc itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct fork-merge-back claim after verification pass\n\nFour parallel research agents fact-checked every citation and claim in\ncloud-native-harness-systems.md against current main. Everything held up\nexcept one: §2 claimed forking's merge strategy is \"hardwired to discard,\"\nbut a real diff-apply ForkMerger already promotes a preserved fork's\nchanges into the parent, default-on when wired (ADR 0039) for Parallel's\nsingle-branch winner. Correct the claim to the actual, narrower scope:\none merge strategy (promote-on-success via diff-apply), wired for exactly\none path, with every other fork path (Team, multi-branch Parallel, and the\nwritable Subagent's deliberately fork-free direct-write mode, ADR 0041)\nstill discarding or bypassing forking entirely. Also tightens two smaller\nimprecisions: the Fork() signature's omitted advisory return, and the\ngit-worktree threat-model rationale's exact source comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
