          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4b0ad1617f3aba3a6b7843d1e51651b09af33ada",
          "message": "fix(deps): bump go1.26.5 + goldmark v1.7.17 to clear govulncheck gate (#254)\n\nCI's govulncheck gate is red on main with three reachable vulnerabilities\nin the root module (the engine module is clean):\n\n  - GO-2026-4970  os root escape via symlink plus trailing slash (stdlib)\n  - GO-2026-5856  crypto/tls ECH privacy leak                  (stdlib)\n  - GO-2026-5320  goldmark XSS                                 (yuin/goldmark)\n\nAll three have upstream fixes, so this bumps rather than allowlists:\n\n  - go directive 1.26 -> 1.26.5 in BOTH modules (root + engine),\n    pulling the fixed crypto/tls + os. setup-go provisions the pinned\n    toolchain via go-version-file, so CI picks this up with no workflow\n    change.\n  - github.com/yuin/goldmark v1.7.8 -> v1.7.17 (transitive via\n    charm.land/glamour/v2, reachable in cmd/mecatui/ui markdown render).\n\nAlso drops the stale GO-2026-4887/GO-2026-4883 args from the Taskfile\n task (CI already runs with no allowlist since toolhive v0.31.0\ncleared the docker/docker vulns); the dead entries caused 'allowlisted\nbut not reachable' warnings on every local run. Syncs the Taskfile desc\nto match the CI job's empty-allowlist posture.\n\nVerified: task vuln (both modules PASS), task build, task lint (0 issues),\ntask test (-race), go run ./cmd/mecademo (full offline session).",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-13T11:33:33+03:00",
