          "id": "182beff390d1da8edb6caca16763cb1e35925a71",
          "message": "feat: scheduled tasks v2 finish — Create form, NL→cron, sched-- GC, one-shot retry, carried context (#189, #236) (#256)\n\n* feat(mecatui): scheduled tasks Phase 3b — in-overlay Create form + NL to cron (#236)\n\nWave 1 of the scheduled-tasks v2 finish (#189 + #236).\n\n- cmd/mecatui/schedparse: a small stdlib-only NL-to-cron compiler (~10 regex\n  patterns: \"every 30 minutes\" to star/30 cron, \"daily at 9am\", \"every weekday\n  at 9am\", \"next monday 3pm\" one-shot, \"in 2 hours\" one-shot, \"tomorrow at\n  noon\" one-shot). NOT a full NLP engine; unmatched input falls back to raw cron.\n- cmd/mecatui/ui/schedule.go: a scheduleCreate sub-view (peer of\n  inspect/confirm) with fields for name, prompt, trigger (cron OR NL),\n  workspace, and a mutating toggle. The c action key opens it; tab/arrows\n  cycle focus; enter submits via CreateScheduleCmd. The trigger field runs\n  schedparse.Compile first, falling back to raw cron.\n- Tests: form open/submit/cancel, NL trigger compilation, validation.\n- Docs: PRODUCTION-READINESS.md flips Phase 3b to shipped; tui.md adds the\n  Create form and NL trigger documentation.\n\n* feat(scheduler): sched-- GC retention family (#236)\n\nWave 2 of the scheduled-tasks v2 finish (#189 + #236).\n\nLands ADR 0059 decision #7 Phase-2 caveat: fire sessions now carry a\nsched-- prefixed id (minted via a WithSessionID override on\nCreateSessionWithProfile) and are GC'd on their own retention schedule\ndistinct from normal session retention.\n\n- internal/adapter/server/service.go: CreateSessionOption variadic options\n  pattern (WithSessionID). Zero opts is byte-identical to the old signature;\n  all existing callers compile unchanged. Override validates non-empty + no\n  collision with a live session.\n- internal/app/scheduler_fire.go: makeFireFunc pre-mints the sched-- id via\n  newFireID and passes it as the session-id override. Success path carries\n  the sched-- id as both fire ID and session ID (decision #7).\n- internal/app/childgc.go: scheduleFireRetention GC family. A new\n  scheduleFireSessionPrefixes partition (sched--) so per-fire sessions are\n  swept by the schedule-fire age pass, NOT the main or child pass.\n  sweepScheduleFires (peer of sweepMain: oldest-first, live-skip).\n- internal/app/build.go: Config.ScheduleFireRetention; cmd/mecated +\n  cmd/mecak8s: --schedule-fire-retention flag (default 7d when scheduling\n  is on; 0 = disabled).\n- Tests: session-id override unit tests; GC partition invariants; e2e\n  asserts the fire session id starts with sched--.\n- Docs: ADR 0059 Phase-2 update note; PRODUCTION-READINESS, architecture,\n  implementation-notes, usage updated; llms.txt regenerated.\n\n* feat(scheduler): one-shot crash-loss retry + carried-context toggle (#236)\n\nWave 3 of the scheduled-tasks v2 finish (#189 + #236).\n\nTwo opt-in ScheduleSpec fields that address ADR 0059 consequences:\n\nOne-shot crash-loss retry:\n- engine/port/schedule.go: ScheduleSpec.OneShotRetry +\n  OneShotMaxRetries, ScheduleState.OneShotRetryCount, the optional\n  ScheduleOneShotReArmer interface (type-asserted on the store, like\n  PrunableStore — not a ScheduleStore method, so existing implementers\n  stay compliant). Rejected on cron triggers (a cron self-heals via\n  misfire).\n- internal/adapter/scheduler/scheduler.go: maybeReArmOneShots scans for\n  disabled one-shots with OneShotRetry=true whose prior fire crashed\n  (LastFireSessionID==pending or LoadFire returns StopError) and re-arms\n  them up to OneShotMaxRetries via ReArmOneShot (atomic re-enable +\n  NextFireAt advance + retry-count increment).\n- All three store adapters implement ReArmOneShot; conformance suite has\n  the atomicity sub-test.\n\nCarried-context toggle:\n- engine/port/schedule.go: ScheduleSpec.CarryContext (default false =\n  fresh per fire, unchanged).\n- internal/app/scheduler_fire.go: when CarryContext is true, the fire\n  path loads the prior fire's session and renders its conversation as a\n  FENCED untrusted preamble (via agent.FenceUntrusted +\n  NeutraliseFraming), prepended to the fire's prompt. NOT seeded history\n  — carried context is untrusted (a prior fire may have been\n  prompt-injected) and must not become live instructions. A re-armed\n  one-shot does NOT carry context on the retry.\n\nAPI-compat gate: task api:update + engine/CHANGELOG.md (Added = minor).\nProto: task generate (new optional fields on ScheduleSpec/ScheduleState).\n\nTests: 5 re-arm tests (pending crash, StopError, no-retry, budget\nexhausted, no-interface degradation); 3 carried-context tests (fence\nrendering, forged-fence neutralisation, disabled-by-default).\n\nDocs: ADR 0059 Phase-2 amendment notes; PRODUCTION-READINESS,\narchitecture, implementation-notes, usage updated; llms.txt regenerated.\n\n* fix(scheduler): address PR #256 review feedback (#236)\n\nResolves the CHANGES_REQUESTED review on the scheduled-tasks v2 finish,\nplus the follow-on review panel's confirmed findings.\n\nReviewer findings:\n- scheduler: run the one-shot crash-loss re-arm scan on EVERY tick, before\n  the len(due)==0 early return, so a quiet one-shot-only deployment (no due\n  cron to \"spark\" the tick) still re-arms a crashed one-shot; bound the\n  LoadFire probe with the tick ctx (singletonTrialTimeout) instead of\n  context.Background().\n- mecatui: surface a failed schedule Create (bad cron / duplicate name /\n  validation error) via actionErr instead of silently closing the form.\n- server: fix the WithSessionID collision check — a reservedIDs in-flight\n  set + a store Load probe close the TOCTOU and the shared-engine fast-path\n  no-op; reject WithSessionID(\"\") per its documented contract.\n- scheduler_fire: rune-accurate carried-context budget; sanitize the\n  schedule name embedded in the fire/session id (control/slash/space runes).\n- childgc: add the symmetric --schedule-fire-retention-max-total count cap\n  (peer of --main-retention-max-total) so a high-frequency cron cannot grow\n  the store's head unbounded within the age horizon.\n\nReview-panel findings:\n- childgc: collapse sweepFamily/sweepMain/sweepScheduleFires into one\n  sweepPartition helper (the hand-copied cap pass was the drift class the\n  extraction prevents); modernize the comparator to slices.SortStableFunc.\n- server: guard CreateSchedule against a duplicate name (Save is upsert-by-\n  name; a Create must not silently clobber an existing task).\n- tests: de-vacuum the carried-context rune-budget test (lower-bound\n  assertion), add a concurrent-create TOCTOU test under -race, add a\n  Load-probe infra-fault propagation test, add a duplicate-name test.\n- accurate \"already in use\" collision message; align actionErr terminal\n  sanitization across both sinks; de-reference ephemeral review comments.\n\ntask build / lint / test (root + engine + engine-standalone) / api:check /\ndocs all green; go run ./cmd/mecademo prints a full offline session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B4zezZnJF9NyFf7KYxu6E9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
