          "message": "test(catalog): replace hardcoded count guards with embedded-bytes fidelity (#312)\n\nThe weekly catalog-refresh re-pin (#310) broke CI because\nTestCuratedModelCounts pinned hardcoded per-provider floor/ceiling\ncounts (openai floor: 50) that went stale the moment models.dev\nlegitimately dropped models (openai 56 -> 47). A specific number for a\nscheduled, upstream-driven value is guaranteed to rot.\n\nReplace it with TestCuratedModelFidelity: decode the raw embedded JSON\nand assert the parsed catalog's per-provider count and model-id set\nmatch the embedded bytes exactly. This keeps the \"no silent caps\"\nintent (a model dropped on the parse floor still diverges loudly) while\nderiving the expectation from the data itself, so a legitimate upstream\nadd/remove never fails spuriously.\n\nUpdate the two stale references to \"floor/ceiling count guards\" in\ncatalog-refresh.yml and IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES.md.",
