          "id": "808aed6b3e8977db8587ebd462e7f57306078ed3",
          "message": "fix(sse): share keepalive filtering across OpenAI adapters (#352)\n\n* fix(sse): share keepalive filtering across OpenAI adapters\n\nExtract the keepalive guard into a shared internal adapter and install it on both Chat Completions and Responses clients.\n\nDrop complete data-less SSE frames so metadata cannot leak into the next event, preserve valid LF and CRLF bytes, and retain bounded-memory and no-progress guards.\n\nFail Responses streams closed when EOF arrives without a terminal event, preventing partial text from being promoted to a successful turn. Add real SDK and constructor regressions and update the living provider docs.\n\nFixes #351\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(openai): add missing trailing blank line to keepalive fixture\n\nThe fixture ended right after the final response.completed data line\nwith no closing blank line, so the openai-go SDK's line-scanner (which\nonly dispatches on an explicit blank line) never emitted the terminal\nevent — CI's Test (race) job failed with a truncated-stream error.\nOther fixtures already end with the required trailing blank line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
