          "message": "feat(mecated): import Codex and Claude Code sessions, skills, and files (#394)\n\n* feat(mecated): import Codex and Claude Code data\n\n* feat(mecated): wire import command\n\n* docs: explain external agent imports\n\n* docs: add external import guide\n\n* docs: refresh llms index\n\n* fix(mecated): harden import command from panel review\n\nAddress findings from a thorough panel review (security, architecture,\nlibrary-reuse, QA test-adequacy, standards) of the import feature:\n\n- SECURITY: guard skill-name path traversal in CopySkillSources — skip any\n  entry named \".\"/\"..\" or containing a path separator so a crafted source\n  dir cannot escape the destination confinement (isSafeSkillName, matching\n  the safeAgentMemoryDir token discipline).\n- lint: decompose runImport (gocyclo 35) into buildImportRequest +\n  performImport and copyTree (gocyclo 27) into planCopy + executeCopy,\n  matching the sibling-subcommand thin-wrapper pattern.\n- lint: doc-comment the exported Source consts (revive); lowercase the\n  \"mecatl session already exists\" error (ST1005).\n- immutability: appendTextMessage no longer mutates session.Message.Text in\n  place (Message is an immutable value object); coalescing builds a fresh\n  message instead.\n- drop the single-caller speculative CopySkills wrapper; test\n  CopySkillSources directly.\n- tests: cross-source skill collision, \"..\"-named skill dir, no-importable-\n  text error, malformed JSONL line, destination-inside-source guard.\n- docs: --skills trust-boundary note (imported skills steer the model like\n  AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md); ADR 0099 records the lossy provider-neutral\n  text-only import decision; regenerate llms.txt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <ozz@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: Juan Antonio Osorio <jaosorior@gmail.com>",
