          "id": "cbf200c6af93046562dc8cb7656ee072b03006a6",
          "message": "feat(provider): cache the conversation, not just the system prefix (ADR 0100) (#416)\n\nThe anthropic adapter placed a single cache_control breakpoint on the\nStablePrefix system block, so only tools+system were cached and every turn\nre-paid full input price for the entire conversation. In an agentic loop the\nmessages are the tokens. The openai (Responses) and openaichat (Chat\nCompletions) adapters sent no cache hints at all, so Claude and Qwen models\nrouted through OpenRouter — which rides the openai adapter — got zero caching.\n\nAnthropic now spends its full 4-slot breakpoint budget: the existing\nStablePrefix marker, a leading-turn-0-fragment anchor (survives compaction), a\nprevious-turn-boundary anchor (guards the 20-block backward lookback, which a\nwide read-parallel fan-out otherwise blows past), and the top-level automatic\nmarker that self-advances to the last cacheable block every turn. Every marker\ncarries the same TTL, which makes the documented TTL-ordering 400s unreachable.\n\nopenai/openaichat gain a (providerID, resolvedBaseURL)-gated cache dialect:\nprompt_cache_key, model-gated prompt_cache_retention for real OpenAI, and\nOpenRouter's request-root cache_control. Gating on the provider id alone would\nbe wrong — an operator can point the openai id at vLLM/LiteLLM — so a\nnon-canonical base URL degrades to no hints at all, and a strict\nOpenAI-compatible upstream can never 400 on a cost optimisation.\ncache_write_tokens is read off the Responses usage raw JSON into the existing\nsession.Usage.CacheWriteTokens, clamped so it stays a subset of InputTokens.\n\nport.LLMRequest is untouched — every knob is an adapter-construction Option.\nDefaults keep the pre-change wire: caching on, no ttl field emitted. New\n--no-prompt-cache and --anthropic-cache-ttl (5m|1h) on mecated, mecatui, and\nmecak8s.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
