          "id": "f85f0c8641be586c189eb2b5ffa83e906670a728",
          "message": "Router: expose routing miss/gate reason on delegation-start events (#397) (#408)\n\n* feat(router): expose routing miss/gate reason on delegation-start events (#397)\n\nThe delegation-start events (EvSubagentStart, parallel branch_start, team\nroster) carried only the router-HIT half (routed_category/routed_model);\nevery miss/gate collapsed to empty strings while the *why* existed only in\noperator diagnostics. A UI could not distinguish router-disabled, pinned\nmodel, agent-def pinned, inherited default, classifier failure, or\nbreaker-open.\n\nPlumb the already-returned missReason through the internal routeTask seam\nand add a bounded, additive routing_reason to the three session payloads +\nthree proto fields (Subagent 18, TeamMemberSpec 8, Parallel 25) + server\nmappers. Empty on a routed hit; a session.RoutingReason* gate constant\n(pinned-model / agent-def-pinned-model / resume / fork / router-disabled /\nbreaker-open / aborted) or a classifier/composition miss string otherwise.\nGauntlet-#7 safe (never the task prompt or classifier reasoning), clamped\nat the emit site. Widens only the internal routeTask + MemberRouting (2->3);\nDeps.SubagentModelRouter is untouched. ADR 0083.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\n\n* fix(router): follow-up repairs for routing_reason on delegation-start (#397)\n\nAddresses the follow-up review findings on the routing-reason feature:\nmecatui now projects routing_reason across Subagent/Parallel/Team render\npaths, Subagent attribution correctly prioritizes explicit resume/fork/\nper-call-model/agent-def choices over router absence, the CHANGELOG entries\nare reclassified under the correct Added/Changed headings, ADR 0083 and the\ndoc lifecycle are filled in, and routingReasonPayload now emits only bounded\nstatic codes (never raw composition/callback text) to close a gauntlet-#7\ngap. Also regenerates engine/api/agent.txt and engine/api/session.txt for\nWithPinnedAgents and RoutingReasonTargetUnavailable, which were added by\nthis diff but missing from the api-compat snapshot.\n\nFixes #397\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(router): address PR #408 review non-blocking notes\n\nAdd a composition-level e2e test proving buildModelRouterTask's\ndetailed category-selector-empty miss reduces to the static wire code\nbefore reaching a delegation-start event, closing the previously\nindirect composition-to-wire seam. Also fix two cosmetic CHANGELOG.md\nformatting issues (a merged bullet, a dropped blank line).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(server): allowlist RoutingReason in the UTF8 structural guard\n\nRebasing 396-sse-missing-on-run onto main surfaced a gap the\nstructural UTF8 fuzz test (added upstream after this branch forked)\nflags automatically: Subagent/Team/Parallel RoutingReason is\nharness/composition-authored bare metadata reduced to a closed\nallowlist (routingReasonPayload), never producer text, so it belongs\nin harnessTokenFields alongside the sibling RoutedCategory/RoutedModel\nfields rather than through valid().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate llms.txt against the fully rebased tree\n\nThe rebase onto origin/main (which had just merged PR #428's llms.txt\nregen) resolved the llms.txt conflict by taking main's side verbatim,\nbut that snapshot predates this branch's own docs/adr/0083 and other\nrouter-reason doc additions being re-applied on top. Regenerate for\nreal against the final tree; task docs:check --strict passes clean\n(0 broken links/anchors/ambiguous/orphans).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <mecatl@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
