          "id": "322ca5104a7a3f788b69475e66ee9428469757bf",
          "message": "skills: close agentskills.io spec-conformance gaps in the metadata/discovery surface (#423)\n\n* feat(skills): parse advisory frontmatter fields onto SkillMeta\n\nParse the agentskills.io optional frontmatter fields license,\ncompatibility, metadata, and allowed-tools (WS3 + WS2 of #419), and\ncarry them on tool.SkillMeta as advisory metadata — path-free, never\ntrust-bearing.\n\n- Skill/SkillMeta/frontmatter gain License, Compatibility, Metadata,\n  AllowedTools; ParseSkill clamps each defensively (it rides the\n  always-in-context tool spec).\n- Skill.Execute surfaces a Compatibility note and an allowed-tools\n  advisory note on activation; the note states calls still follow normal\n  permission rules. allowed-tools is ADVISORY ONLY — it never feeds the\n  permission evaluator (deny-dominance invariant holds at every posture;\n  pinned by TestAllowedToolsDoesNotBypassPolicy).\n- Driver proto SkillMeta gains license/compatibility/metadata/\n  allowed_tools (fields 5-8); grpcdriver client re-clamps hostile wire\n  data to the parser's caps; server projects the fields.\n- sourceconformance Fixture widened so every SkillSource backend\n  round-trips the new fields.\n\napi: engine/api/tool.txt refreshed (SkillMeta widened, Added/minor).\n\n* feat(skills): validate discovered skill names + require dir-name match\n\nWS4 of #419. Discovery now validates a skill's name against the shared\ngrammar and requires it to match the parent directory name, both\nfail-soft (SkipError, scan continues).\n\n- New shared validator skillfs.ValidSkillName implements the lax grammar\n  ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$ — underscore deliberately ALLOWED (the\n  grammar the draft write path already used); discovery previously\n  accepted any non-empty name. The lax form is pinned by\n  TestDiscoveryAcceptsUnderscoreNames as a tripwire against a future\n  tightening.\n- ParseSkill rejects a grammar-failing name (fatal skip).\n- DirSource.Skills enforces the dir-name-match rule (frontmatter name ==\n  parent dir), replacing the documented \"frontmatter name wins\" behavior.\n- The draft write path routes validateName through the same shared\n  ValidSkillName (behavior unchanged; the local regex is removed).\n\n* feat(skills): enumerate bundled assets on activation\n\nWS1 of #419. The agentskills.io \"enumerate bundled scripts/resources but\ndo not eagerly read them\" contract: Skill.Execute now renders a sorted\n\"Bundled files:\" block listing each asset's logical name, without reading\npayloads (a counting ReadSkillAsset test pins zero reads on activation).\n\n- Activation gains an Assets []tool.SkillAsset field, populated by both\n  the snapshot activator (FS, in place) and the source activator (driver,\n  cached). The port tool.SkillSource is unchanged (ListSkillAssets\n  already existed).\n- The enumeration is gated on len(Assets) > 0 so an asset-less skill\n  renders byte-identically to before (the existing golden stays green);\n  new golden sub-tests pin the enumeration block and the combined\n  block ordering byte-for-byte.\n\n* feat(skills): expose discovered skills as /skill-name slash commands\n\nWS5 of #419. Each discovered skill is now invocable as /<skill-name>,\nexpanding to the skill body injected directly as the user prompt\n(Claude-Code skill-as-command semantics), by bridging the skill seam into\nthe existing prompt.CommandSource/SourceExpander layer — no new tool, no\nnew dispatch concept.\n\n- New engine/adapter/skillfs.SkillCommandSource implements\n  prompt.CommandSource over the skill seam (metas + Activator);\n  ListCommands projects each skill (ValidCommandName-filtered, sorted);\n  CommandBody returns the already-frontmatter-stripped body via Activate.\n- buildCommandExpander composes it with precedence\n  dirExp > skillExp > sourceExp > mcpExp (a local command file shadows a\n  same-named skill; a skill shadows a driver command). The project-tier\n  trust gate is inherited by construction — an untrusted workspace's\n  project skills are never discovered, so they are never invocable.\n- Also fixes a latent driver bug the review panel caught: the grpcdriver\n  client ListSkillAssets now sorts by name (FS parity); the conformance\n  suite previously masked the omission by sorting both sides before\n  comparing. Regression test TestSkillSourceListAssetsSortsHostileOrder\n  fails without the fix.\n\nDocs: usage + user-docs document /skill-name; llms.txt regenerated.\n\n* fix(skills): wire the grpcdriver client round-trip for advisory fields\n\nThe WS3/WS2 work added the proto SkillMeta fields (5-8) and the server\nprojection, but the driver's client ListSkills never mapped\nLicense/Compatibility/Metadata/AllowedTools off the wire — they were\nsilently dropped. The grpcdriver conformance + round-trip tests caught it\nunder `go test -race` in CI (a stale local test cache had masked it).\n\n- ListSkills now maps the four advisory fields, re-clamped defensively to\n  the parser's caps (clampAdvisoryString/clampAdvisoryMetadata/\n  clampAllowedTools) so a hostile/buggy driver cannot bloat the\n  always-in-context tool spec.\n- ListSkillAssets now name-sorts its result for FS-source parity (the\n  Skill tool's \"Bundled files:\" enumeration renders in this order); the\n  conformance suite had masked the omission by sorting both sides.\n\nFixes the CI Test (race) failure on #423.\n\n* fix(skills): harden slash activation\n\nMake asset-bearing skill slash commands render bounded activation metadata after command-template substitution, preserving literal asset paths and existing tool output order. Validate driver-supplied skill and asset identities before they reach model-facing prompts or cache paths.\n\nAffected components: skillfs activation, prompt command expansion, SkillSource validation, grpcdriver, asset materialization, docs, and API compatibility.\n\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl <noreply@mecatl.dev>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jakub Hrozek <jakub@stacklok.com>\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@mecatl.dev>",
