          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8fa6168c1176ec2a0d3df3dec303920e4b5b4d8f",
          "message": "docs(adr)+test(mecatui): post-merge review follow-up to #463 (#474)\n\n* refactor(cliconfig): share the prompt/prompt-file join across both mains\n\ncmd/mecatui/prompt.go landed as a byte-for-byte copy of\ncmd/mecatequi/prompt.go's joinPromptBody -- same body, same doc comment.\nBoth mains must agree on the join (\"literal first, blank line between,\ntrailing newlines trimmed\") because they expose the same two flags, and\ninternal/cliconfig exists for exactly this class: \"the small slices of\nCLI/composition wiring that the four command mains would otherwise\ncopy-paste -- extracted here so they cannot drift apart.\"\n\nHoist it to cliconfig.JoinPromptBody and delete both local copies. The\ntable test moves with it, so it now covers mecatequi's path too --\npreviously mecatequi's copy had no test at all, which is what made the\nduplication a real drift risk rather than a cosmetic one.\n\nNo behaviour change: the function body is unchanged, and mecatequi's\nbuildPrompt still layers its trusted-instructions / untrusted-fence\nwrapping on top of the joined body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(mecatui): fix a runDone data race and collapse the seed-test copies\n\nThree findings from a review of #463, all in cmd/mecatui/ui/ui_test.go.\n\n1. progress.runDone was read WITHOUT prog.mu at two seed assertions while\n   the reducer goroutine writes it under the lock in record(). Both reads\n   happen with the program still live, so -race can flag them; the run\n   passing today is timing, not safety. Fixed at the shared type with a\n   guarded runs() accessor rather than per call site, so a future\n   upper-bound assertion cannot reintroduce it. Its doc comment records\n   why the reads looked safe: waitRunComplete establishes only the LOWER\n   bound, so \"exactly n, no more\" needs the locked read.\n\n2. newSeedProgramModel was a 25-line fork of newProgramModel differing\n   only by Deps.InitialPrompt (and an omitted onSend release hook that is\n   inert with gateType \"\"), and TestSeedPromptConnectFallbackFires\n   inlined a THIRD copy of the same construction. newProgramModel now\n   takes tweak ...func(*Deps); the six pre-existing call sites are\n   untouched, newSeedProgramModel becomes a 3-line delegation, and the\n   fallback test builds through the helper.\n\n3. Four added copies of the frames()->GetPrompt() filter loop are\n   replaced by the promptTexts helper that ALREADY existed in the package\n   (queue_test.go) -- the loops also bound a p they never used.\n\nTest-only; no production code touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(adr): record the mecatui seed-prompt decisions as ADR 0103\n\n#463 shipped -p/--prompt + --prompt-file but recorded the WHY only in code\ncomments and operator prose. AGENTS.md's documentation lifecycle makes the\nwhy of a feature a frozen ADR, and this feature made four decisions a\nfuture reader will otherwise re-litigate:\n\n- interactive-seed, NOT print-and-exit (that need is mecatequi's, ADR\n  0028; a one-shot mode in the TUI would need a second render path)\n- the seed rides the IDENTICAL typed-prompt path, which is why a\n  /-prefixed seed is intercepted locally and a --prompt-file body carries\n  full typed-prompt authority -- both accepted rather than special-cased\n- fires exactly once, enforced structurally (one consume site, cleared\n  before submit) across /models, /clear and the connect-fallback rebind\n- the literal-then-file join order, now shared via cliconfig\n\nConsequences also records the costs the same review surfaced and did not\nfix: applySessionReady's contract is now wider than its name (it can start\na run, and its one wrapping caller post-mutates the returned model), -p and\n--prompt share a destination so passing both silently keeps the last, flag\nparsing now performs I/O, the file read is unbounded, and a --prompt-file\nwhose content the operator did not author inherits @-expansion authority.\n\nAdds the docs/adr/README.md index entry (matlatl check --strict reports the\nADR unreachable without it) and the living per-subsystem mechanics section\nin IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES next to the CLI transport grammar entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(adr): correct two seed-prompt claims ADR 0103 inherited from a comment\n\nA panel review of the follow-up branch caught two factual errors in the\nfreshly-written ADR 0103 and its IMPLEMENTATION-NOTES section.\n\n1. /clear does NOT re-enter applySessionReady. runClear (builtins.go)\n   resets the conversation on the SAME session via resetSession and never\n   reaches that seam; only a /models restart and the connect-fallback\n   rebind do. The \"fires exactly once, enforced structurally\" argument\n   therefore named a path it was never checked against -- harmless\n   behaviourally (the field is cleared before submitPrompt either way),\n   but the claim was wrong. ROOT CAUSE: the ADR reproduced the code\n   comment shipped in #463 (update.go, \"a /models restart or /clear, both\n   of which funnel back through here\") rather than the code, so the\n   comment is corrected too -- fixing only the ADR would have left the\n   same wrong sentence in the source for the next reader to copy.\n\n2. submitPrompt has THREE input-preserving loud-reject early returns\n   (ExpandMentions, StageClipboardImage, CheckAggregateCaps), not four.\n   The fourth candidate (the \"open run:\" arm) returns endRun(stopError)\n   after the textarea was already reset -- not the same class.\n\nAlso drops a line-number citation in ui_test.go (update.go:364) for the\nsymbol it meant, which does not rot on the next edit above it.\n\nDocs and comments only; no behaviour change. task lint is 0 issues and\ndocs/lint (the citation gate) passes with the new builtins.go citation.\n\nNOTE: llms.txt is NOT regenerated in this commit -- matlatl is\nunreachable from this environment. The edits touch only prose inside\nexisting sections (no headings, no links), so the index is expected to be\nunchanged, but run `task docs` before relying on that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
