          "id": "e185c1b41b43967cfeb6ec9a1c6e038d50f9980c",
          "message": "feat(mecatui): wrap + scroll permission-modal args, full-screen ask-args view (#488) (#553)\n\nThe permission modal rendered a non-diff ask's args as one unwrapped\npretty-JSON blob, so a long Bash command ran off the approval card and\nthe operator authorized commands they could not read.\n\nTwo tiers now: the modal's args region soft-wraps (ansi.Wrap + Hardwrap\nbackstop) into a capped mini-viewport (10 rows; arrows/pgup/pgdn + wheel\nover the card scroll it; a fixed hint line advertises ctrl+t full args),\nand ctrl+t routes by ask type — non-diff asks open a full-screen\nscrollable ask-args view (argsVP, mirroring the plan-review pattern) with\nthe generic verdict buttons pinned; Edit/Write keep the in-modal diff\nexpand; plan asks untouched. Verdict keys fire from inside the view;\nesc/ctrl+t return to the modal. A rebindable RawArgs key (default bare r)\ntoggles pretty (decoded {\"command\":...} + muted timeout_ms annotation)\nvs raw (the VERBATIM sanitized wire string — the approval-integrity\nfloor). The command renders in a bright askArgs style with a\ntool-coloured left accent bar; a soft wrap carries a warning-coloured\ntrailing ↩; the card sizes to content up to 132 columns and stays put\nwhile scrolling (the block width pins to the widest line over the whole\ncontent, not the visible window).\n\nClick geometry is a region-emitting registry (the click half of #555):\neach approval surface's regions are computed from the SAME layout\nbuilders the render path uses, with the buttonsRow travelling inside the\nbuilder's return value — one source, no skew; clickAt looks up,\ndispatchClick executes, and the wheel gate + hit-test share one\napprovalCardRect. MECATUI_DEBUG_ASK=1 registers an env-gated /debug-ask\nbuiltin (never a --help flag) cycling three canned long-args asks through\nthe real reducer; a debug ask resumes the phase it interrupted\n(askResumePhase) rather than a dead running phase. ADR 0108 records the\nctrl+t routing rule, the raw/pretty tier decision, and the wrap-marker\nconvention.\n\nCo-authored-by: mecatl <noreply@stacklok.com>",
