          "id": "af187549adee8b4c2f177d8e253444262ee44eb6",
          "message": "fix(mecatui): re-capture selBase when a selection gesture races a delta (#571) (#572)\n\nWhile a response streams, clicking/dragging to select text in the\nscrollback flashed the viewport back to an earlier, shorter conversation\nstate for as long as the gesture continued.\n\nsnapshotSelection splices the selection highlight onto selBase, a cached\nunstyled render of the conversation that was only refreshed inside\nrefreshView. A streamed delta does not re-render immediately — it sets\nviewDirty and defers the flush to the frame-cadence renderTickMsg. A\ngesture landing in the window after a delta arrived but before the tick\nfired re-spliced the stale, shorter selBase and SetContent it, reverting\nthe viewport to the pre-delta conversation.\n\nRe-capture selBase from the live conversation in snapshotSelection\nwhenever viewDirty is set, so the splice always starts from current\ncontent. This reuses the existing renderConversation chokepoint (off the\nstreaming hot path) and deliberately avoids refreshView, which would\nclear viewDirty, run GotoBottom, and could drop the selection mid-drag.\n\nRegression: TestGestureInDirtyWindowDoesNotFlashBack drives a drag inside\nthe dirty window and asserts the viewport retains the in-flight delta\n(fails without the fix, passes with it).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
