          "id": "aacf0d0cbed3ff3799cb7dda6e6e924819229bb5",
          "message": "fix(ci): use an iteration count for fuzz-smoke, not a wall-clock deadline (#680)\n\n* fix(ci): use an iteration count for fuzz-smoke, not a wall-clock deadline\n\nFuzzCanonicalize intermittently failed with \"context deadline exceeded\" at\nthe -fuzztime boundary on loaded runners, even after doubling the budget\nfrom 20s to 40s. A duration budget races go test's own fuzz coordinator\nnear the deadline; an iteration count (Nx) has no deadline to race, so the\nsmoke job stops after a fixed number of executions regardless of runner\nspeed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): give the Test (race) job real timeout headroom\n\nThe last 8 successful runs on main all took 14m17s-14m51s against a 15m\ncap -- no slack, so ordinary runner-load variance tips it over (as seen\non this PR). Bump to 20m.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
