          "id": "ff9089e3b3f1d80fea879713d658143dadbfc2b6",
          "message": "mecatui: make --resume-latest fall back to new when none eligible (#754)\n\n* mecatui: add --resume-latest-or-new (resume newest eligible chat or start new)\\n\\n- Add --resume-latest-or-new: try newest eligible owned main chat; if none exists, start a fresh chat.\\n- Mutually exclusive with --resume / --resume-latest; conflicts with sessions browser and seed-prompt flags.\\n- Tests: flag grammar, adopt-on-hit, fallback-on-miss, list-failure still errors.\\n- Docs: docs/tui.md, docs/usage.md, user-docs/mecatui/sessions.md.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl agent <agent@local>\n\n* mecatui: make --resume-latest fall back to new when none eligible\\n\\n- Drop --resume-latest-or-new flag; default --resume-latest now starts a new chat if no eligible one exists.\\n- Keep list/transport failures as real errors (not masked).\\n- Update tests and docs accordingly.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: mecatl agent <agent@local>\n\n* mecatui: remove unused resumeLatestOrNew field left over from flag removal\n\nThe prior commit dropped the --resume-latest-or-new flag but left the\nconfig struct field and a stale comment reference behind, which the\nCI lint job's unused-field check caught.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
