          "id": "fe4b8917e16b01a6d1a6e0f6dd3ceb240e1e9eae",
          "message": "fix(cut-release): make pin-bump/check scripts macOS-compatible (#773)\n\nDiscovered while cutting v0.0.16: bump-release-pins.sh's `sed -i -E`\nis parsed by BSD sed (macOS's default /bin/sed) as `-i` taking `-E`\nitself as the backup-suffix argument, silently running in basic-regex\nmode, so the `(...)`/`\\1` capture groups fail with \"\\1 not defined in\nthe RE\". check-reusable-pins.sh's `mapfile` is bash 4+ only, but\nmacOS ships bash 3.2 as /bin/bash.\n\n- bump-release-pins.sh: replace both `sed -i -E` calls with\n  `perl -pi -e`, which behaves identically across BSD/GNU/macOS/Linux.\n  OLD_TAG/NEW_TAG cross via %ENV, never interpolated into the regex or\n  replacement source.\n- check-reusable-pins.sh: replace `mapfile -t` with a portable\n  while-read-into-array loop.\n\nVerified against an isolated copy of the real pin files with macOS's\nstock /bin/bash + /usr/bin/sed: bump-release-pins.sh v9.9.9 correctly\nrewrites all 4 pin occurrences and the gate's own self-check passes.\nNo change to behavior on Linux/CI (already-modern bash/GNU sed there).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-27T08:53:38+02:00",
          "tree_id": "36cd1c5959b08c266b0dd607c8f7e45c359779ec",
          "url": "https://github.com/stacklok/mecatl/commit/fe4b8917e16b01a6d1a6e0f6dd3ceb240e1e9eae"
